context:
{'name': 'Muddy Waters Cafe', 'address': '508 E Haley St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Jazz & Blues, Music Venues, Arts & Entertainment, Nightlife, Restaurants, Bars, Local Flavor, Bagels, Food, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Dive Bars, Delis, Coffee & Tea', 'hours': {'Monday': '6:0-18:0', 'Tuesday': '6:0-18:0', 'Wednesday': '6:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '6:0-18:0', 'Friday': '6:0-18:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-18:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2015-09-18 02:36:39', 'review_text': "So sad to hear Muddy's is closing . Great coffee house, eclectic art and people! Not sure where my go to place will be now......"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-08-09 20:19:08', 'review_text': 'So many little spaces, rooms, and nooks to sit on a chair, couch or table.  Perfect for working, meeting up with friends, hanging out.  Great inside and outside space.  Art focused, which I LOVE!

If I lived closer, this would be a regular spot.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2015-05-29 06:16:17', 'review_text': 'Decent coffee at an okay price. Some people like the decorations but I thought it was kind of messy and had a grandma-esque vibe too it. 

I got my usual, an iced coffee and HOT DAMN. It was strong...like a too strong for my tastes. I will come back to try their other drinks though. Not giving up on this place just yet!'}]}

{'name': 'El Taco Tequila Taqueria', 'address': '14 E Cota St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Mexican', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': True, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2013-12-06 03:03:14', 'review_text': "On Thursday night I went to this place after a concert. A few friends and I wanted a bite and a drink. We ordered with a young woman who quickly told us they did not accommodate gluten free customers, even if you wanted a taco or tostada without the bread. Fine. I'll work around that I understand. We waited 20 minutes for our food, granted there was only one guy in the kitchen. We finally got our tacos and were missing one chicken taco and our guacamole. We ask the chef for the rest of our order and he says they are closing the kitchen. I go to the woman and tell her that we didn't get all our food and she tells me I'm lying. I point to the plates on our table to show her we didn't. I ask for our money back and she declines. We end up getting into a fight about one chicken taco and guac. 

I have worked in restaurants before and I would never scold a customer over a $3 taco. I even offed to pay for it and she wouldn't let me. Really terrible customer service. The chef did make us some guac bc I think he felt bad that we were hungry and upset. By that point we had eaten what we were served and didn't have anything to put it on.

That being said the food we get was yummy. Too bad our experience ended on such a bad note."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2013-03-28 15:50:04', 'review_text': "We both got food poisoning here - that lasted a whole day. We narrowed it down to either the chips & salsa, the queso app, or the carnitas tacos since that's the only thing BOTH of us ate. The food seemed great, but it seems to be all about pushing the drinks for $$ and food safety was left to the sidelines."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2012-11-03 03:56:19', 'review_text': 'Great food. WOnderful atmosphere. Great Happy hour two for one Margaritas. I love the decor too. Beautiful Bar. Amazing flan!'}]}

{'name': "Pollofino's", 'address': '6831 Hollister Ave', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Mexican', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-21:0', 'Friday': '11:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': None, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-03-29 15:50:33', 'review_text': 'Pretty overpriced for a small portion of average quality food.




-'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-02-11 16:16:53', 'review_text': "3 stars
It's not that bad as a resturaunt the service is fine and the food comes at a good speed and you can maybe hear a sizzle in the kitchen. the quesadillas are good and so are the burritos but the tomatoes really overpower the other flavors which I don't like and the guacamole is sad and bland, If you buy a container of guacamole its not worth it because it is overpriced for the size and it tastes very sad and bland like it was just mourning a dead relative. Overall not bad I guess may eat there again. Don't judge the resturaunt completely off my rating because it is very good there is just some things I dont like."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-12-27 04:08:53', 'review_text': 'Simply the best most delicious chicken and tri tip in town. Great prices too & dependable quality. The char chicken burrito deluxe is my staple although the No. 1 Combo and Fajitas are also favorites. You cannot go wrong here. This is the first place I bring my guests to impress. All smiles.'}]}

{'name': 'Itsuki Restaurant', 'address': '4020 Calle Real', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Japanese, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '17:30-21:30', 'Tuesday': '17:30-21:30', 'Wednesday': '17:30-21:30', 'Thursday': '17:30-21:30', 'Friday': '17:30-21:30', 'Saturday': '17:30-21:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2015-05-25 20:54:35', 'review_text': "Absolutely disappointing. As a matter of fact, this experience was so disappointing it caused me to take time out of my very busy life to write my first review ever. 

I'm someone who is happy when there is quantity. So I spend $60 here thinking that should do a good job filling me up (I order the 25$ sashimi bowl and 2 rolls) and I did not get filled up. The sashimi itself disappointed me as well due to the low quantity of cuts compared to kyoto's 25$ bowl. In addition, the fish itself I thought was less fresh. The 2 rolls were also small in comparison to Kyoto's. I'm never coming here again. Man I could have gotten 10 chipotle burrito's with those $60...."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2013-04-23 19:18:42', 'review_text': 'This is the best sushi in Santa Barbara, aside from maybe Arigato, which is absolutely not worth the money. Go, go, go!'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2013-01-09 23:59:06', 'review_text': "The restaurant has located to the Camino Real Marketplace area (actually, more like near Pacific Oaks) in Goleta, where Baja Fresh used to be. The ambiance is *totally* different. It's become a big business. They're still getting the hang of how to serve so many people, and seem always to be apologizing for slow service, when it's actually about the same as other places. 

The food was not great the first few times I went, but the last time...yum...they were back on their game. It's worth a try!"}]}

{'name': 'The Pub', 'address': '224 Helena Ave', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Beer, Wine & Spirits, Pubs, Arts & Entertainment, Gay Bars, Bars, Nightlife, Food, Music Venues', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '16:0-2:0', 'Wednesday': '16:0-2:0', 'Thursday': '16:0-2:0', 'Friday': '16:0-2:0', 'Saturday': '16:0-2:0', 'Sunday': '15:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2014-09-11 03:34:17', 'review_text': 'Sadly, The Pub is "gay for pay." - they only seem to entertain the idea of being gay bar when it suits their bottom line. Also, I don't exactly enjoy hanging out in a bar that's sandwiched between a strip club and an adult book store either. The food is good but overpriced and the drinks are expensive and inconsistent. And what's with the rock hard chairs? The only reason I frequented this establishment is because they claimed to be a gay bar otherwise the quality vs. value quotient just doesn't cut it. The new Pub is doing a disservice to the Legendary "Pub" that was it's predecessor in the same location!'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-08-23 21:59:28', 'review_text': "This was, very briefly, Santa Barbara's only gay bar. The last time we went, we could tell that they had new owners and everything had changed.

The new people behind the bar were nice, we were served in reasonable time, the bar was very quiet and it felt like as if it were just really slow business. Really sad actually, I had high hopes for this place."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-25 23:55:16', 'review_text': 'This place is just okay. Ordered a scotch "neat" and the young bartender had no clue what I meant. I explained it, then he began to condescend to me that drinking that sounds nasty to him...scowling at me the entire time. Wow. Nice move to demean the customer!

It's fine to hang out with a group of friends, but don't get your hopes up. Pretty bland establishment in my opinion...and I love low-key. This is not low-key, it's no-key, if you get my drift.'}]}

{'name': 'The Blue Owl', 'address': '5 W Canon Perdido', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, American (New), Thai, Restaurants, Asian Fusion, Desserts, Cafes, Sandwiches, Caterers, Event Planning & Services', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-20:0', 'Friday': '11:0-2:30', 'Saturday': '11:0-2:30', 'Sunday': '11:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': True, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': None, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-19 05:49:47', 'review_text': 'I got a tofu banh mi, and it was pretty disappointing. The sandwich was fairly small for the price, and the inside of the sandwich was basically empty. Like, if you looked at it from the side, you would think it was just a piece of bread sliced down the middle. Seriously!

To add insult to injury, it tastes *nothing* like a banh mi. They should just call it something else because there was nothing inside that sandwich that tasted anything remotely like a banh mi does.

Three stars because my friend got a turkey sandwich that they really loved, so just averaging out the stars between the two of us.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 18:03:45', 'review_text': "This place slaps! I've lived in SB for 5 years and I hit Blue owls all the time. 10/10 would recommend. Fav is the Rice with pork and spicy chili sauce!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 00:35:57', 'review_text': 'What a great little lunch spot! We dropped by one afternoon and were really pleasantly surprised but the quality of the food. Reasonably priced as well, if you factor in the Santa Barbara "tax". The beet salad was really fresh and flavorful, and don't forget to throw an egg on top of that fried rice! Did I mention they serve beer? Not that you would ever have one during lunchtime...'}]}

{'name': 'Cafe Ana', 'address': '1201 Anacapa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Donuts, Wine Bars, Bars, Breakfast & Brunch, Bakeries, American (New), Nightlife, Food, Coffee & Tea, Restaurants, Cafes', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-04-20 12:02:35', 'review_text': "I've been wanting to check this place out for a little while now, and I finally had the chance to eat brunch here with a couple of friends (before the covid-19 closures). The food was delicious and I personally really loved their pastry basket. I can't wait until it's safe to eat in restaurants again because this is definitely going to be one of the first places I go to! Their pastry case looked amazing and they had so many menu items that intrigued me!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-05-03 23:49:49', 'review_text': 'I hope this place opens soon. I just discovered it and really loved it.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-03-06 10:27:28', 'review_text': "I love this cafe and so easy to run in for lunch while working in county building.  They are always clean and the food is great!  They are quick and friendly.  Their cheeseburger is the best cheeseburger I've had in a long time!
Grilled bun, super melty cheese and thick meat!  Good tomato and sauce is yum.  Love their chips and they make a Bloody Mary too.  There are days you need a bloody Mary to deal with the day.  Then walk back over to county bldg.  

Cafe always has nice staff.  I tip them well.  They make an amazing meal quick and what else can I ask for"}]}

{'name': 'The Bak Door', 'address': '320 S Kellogg Ave', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Dive Bars, Nightlife, Bars', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2011-06-26 07:35:23', 'review_text': "The ultimate dive bar.  Cheap stiff drinks, pool tables, and an awesome juke box.  Don't come here to be wowed, but to relax at the place where you know everyones name."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2010-09-19 16:07:47', 'review_text': "The Bak Dor. I'm with Anne -- refreshing to hit a dive bar that isn't asses to elbows with ironic mustaches, cutoff jeans, and topsiders. 

The staff is friendly, the peanuts and pretzels are free, they have Coors, and they have Hank Williams (Sr) on the juke box. If you are a pool player, the regulars here kept the table going and seemed pretty nice. 

Good spot to grab a drink if you find yourself with a half hour in Goleta."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2009-10-10 19:07:59', 'review_text': 'the two stars bac dor gets are simply because of the sweet, elderly dude behind the bar and the ok jukebox.  despite friends who love bac dor, im NOT enthusiastic about the altercations we get in every single time with angry and drunk-as-shit regulars. imo, there are plenty of other goleta bars that are more fun.  i say let the oldtimers be in peace at bac dor.  the drinks themselves arent cheap either.'}]}

{'name': 'Casa Blanca Restaurant', 'address': '330 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Mexican, Restaurants, Seafood', 'hours': {'Monday': '16:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '16:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '16:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '16:0-22:0', 'Friday': '16:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-0:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2020-03-11 05:59:08', 'review_text': "My friend and I came here for lunch on Saturday. I am not sure how it is at dinner, but for lunch there was no line so it was fast to get a table. The waiter was very thorough and accommodating. Both my friend and I had the blood orange margarita, which was so good because it had a jalapeño kick! But, don't worry it's not too spicy for anyone that is sensitive to spice, it was just right. 

We both ended up going with the combination plate; me the taco and enchilada and her the taco and tamale. To be honest the only reason why I didn't go with the mahi mahi taco was because it was singular (taco) versus the other tacos were plural in the name (tacos) and so I was expecting to get at least two tacos in the combo. However, only one came so I would ask that the menu be more clear. But, the food was delicious and we even had enough for leftovers. Both plates came with rice and beans too. 

There is an axxess deal for BOGO entree for lunch or dinner as well. So with all the food and drinks we had my friend and I were able to split it evenly for about $24 per person, which I think is a great deal for such a quality food."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2020-03-08 15:09:08', 'review_text': "Delicious food and drinks! Really fast service. Nice location with a nice scenic patio. They have heaters so you don't have to worry about getting cold. I ordered the burrito and my husband got the fajitas, both were delicious! I also got the margarita flight, which I highly recommend. If you're close to Amtrak on state, I would recommend stopping by!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-03-01 05:02:35', 'review_text': 'Ate at the bar tonight for my friends birthday. The bartender Dan, (tall, light and handsome) was attentive and took great care of us! Fast drinks with a warm welcoming personality, a great guy. Good food too! my Bf and I had the tacos.. simple but tasty! Thank you!'}]}

{'name': 'Via Vai Trattoria Pizzeria', 'address': '1483 E Valley Rd, Ste 20', 'city': 'Montecito', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Pizza, Restaurants, Italian', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:30-21:0', 'Tuesday': '11:30-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:30-21:0', 'Friday': '11:30-21:30', 'Saturday': '11:30-21:30', 'Sunday': '11:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-16 04:36:01', 'review_text': 'I understand that they are understaffed and the reasons.
We had lunch there last weekend Three of the four lunches were good. My lunch was inedible I ordered grilled Italian sausages with sautéed spinach and polenta. Only the spinach was edible No one came to see if we were happy with our meals.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-05 19:01:57', 'review_text': "The staff could not have been more welcoming on a stormy Santa Barbara evening. Everyone in our party of six was delighted by the food and ambience. This is one of Montecito's treasures!"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-09-13 02:41:36', 'review_text': "Please do not go here ! Absolutely the worst Italian food I've had in years! Meatballs tasted frozen and undercooked. The fish had no flavor. The bread was stale. There was literally nothing that was good. Why they have any customers I honestly cannot say. Believe the other yelp reviews they really are that bad!!!

STAY AWAY"}]}

{'name': 'Montecito Village Grocery', 'address': '1482 E Valley Rd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Specialty Food, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Grocery, Bakeries, Restaurants, Delis, Butcher, Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-20:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-20:0', 'Friday': '7:0-20:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-20:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-15 18:18:53', 'review_text': 'Montecito Village Grocery  was apparently my husband's mother's go-to grocery store. Smaller with less inventory than the big chain groceries in town, but also an easier place to shop, as it never gets crowded. I've been to the Von's on Coast Village Road many times over the years--it's pretty convenient, after all, and impossible to miss if you spend any time in Montecito. By contrast, I'd never even seen this market until Matt B. suggested we go to pick up a few odd things we needed for the week.

It's a cute place with some comfortable neighborhood charm, and I enjoyed the ample parking and calm, quiet atmosphere. Obviously, the stock was more limited than at a supermarket--we couldn't find the pasta we wanted and did end up making a Von's run later in the week--but we picked up some of the items on our list, including a few bottles of wine. The wine selection was solid, with lots of local/regional wines. Definitely extensive enough that you'll walk away with what you need if you're not looking for anything too specific. (Our toddler, who was just learning his colors, pointed to a wall of reds and said, "Red? Red?") The cheese/deli section was pretty enticing, too.

Check-out was quick and easy and we went home with enough provisions to see us through dinner that night (mostly, we needed wine). I like Vons fine, but it's nice to have Montecito Village Grocery as a pleasant, less busy alternative.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-08-08 12:02:22', 'review_text': "Bad service and expired products, its always hit or miss there, your better off going to Von's."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-09-10 15:53:32', 'review_text': "This neighborhood grocery store has awesome European speciality items, not found elsewhere.  From the Deli to yogurt, olives, to plant-based products: it provides quality food at its finest.  We've become accustomed to settle for the adjacent and lower quality in our diets: not cool.  Treat yourself, this grocery store is Delectable."}]}

{'name': 'Union Ale', 'address': '214 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, American (Traditional), Restaurants, Cocktail Bars, Nightlife', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-23:0', 'Friday': '11:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2016-09-23 22:32:27', 'review_text': "2nd transformation in 18 months...same owners, but now it feels like there's even less on the menu, and it's even more disorganized. What remains arrives without salad or fries or even a tidbit of  garnish. Your food comes on a metal tray without napkins or eating tools. If you order a hamburger, expect it to come under a super greasy bun. 

The patio is no longer covered so you'll be sitting in direct sunlight. It feels like this place is having an extended identity crisis. 

Damn if the funk zone doesn't need some decent dependable lunch places. This establishment is really missing out on an easy opportunity here. Great location, nice facility, but no thought or care in what they're serving up or in what they want to be."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2016-01-10 02:25:11', 'review_text': "Horrible service. It took 20 minutes to get a drink order when it wasn't even that busy. Their food is goods"}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2016-01-04 20:55:40', 'review_text': "2 stars for the beer choices which is the only positive remnant of what was one of my go to places downtown. They've all but eliminated all the great food they served. They've now removed all but 2 TVs. Very disappointing business choices. I walked in this past weekend to catch a nationally televised hockey game, something I've done dozens of times here in the past. The bartender acknowledges us but is so busy covering the entire restaurant that he didn't get to us for nearly 10 minutes. We had to walk out and find a more suitable place to catch the game. Can't say I'll have a desire to go back. This town was already lacking decent sports bars with a good beer selection."}]}

{'name': 'Deep Sea Tasting Room', 'address': '217 G Stearns Wharf', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Venues & Event Spaces, Event Planning & Services, Wine Tasting Room, Arts & Entertainment, Food, Wine Bars, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Nightlife, Wineries', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-20:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-20:0', 'Friday': '11:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': True, 'lot': False, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-18 00:53:58', 'review_text': "Beautiful beautiful view and friendly staff. We went on a rainy morning and still enjoyed the view. Wines are serviceable but it's really about the view."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-03 20:29:36', 'review_text': "It's a great location to have a drink. Beautiful views. Good breeze. It's unfortunate that the wine isn't as good as the location."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-01 23:32:42', 'review_text': 'Good Afternoon,

I am again submitting this review in reference to prior feedback i offered regarding an unfortunate very racially charged incident at Deep Sea Tasting room. To date the venue has still made no attempt at reaching out to me to discuss this rather u fortunate encounter with management that resulted in me cancelling my membership and not returning.

I wish the follow-up on the part of the leadership was as good as the view from the tasting room.'}]}

{'name': 'Santa Barbara Wine Spa', 'address': '29 W Micheltorena St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Active Life, Pizza, Beauty & Spas, Restaurants, Day Spas, Golf, Health & Medical', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-21:0', 'Friday': '11:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '12:0-17:0', 'Sunday': '12:0-17:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2017-03-07 04:26:41', 'review_text': 'I was sold a package, business closed, so I'm screwed. That's why I"m updating my review. I'm sure this happened to a lot of other folks too!'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2016-10-24 02:11:25', 'review_text': "+1 (949) 310-7016 is Lauryns Cel number by the way! Good luck getting your refund! 

Jeff was the best part of that place . I guess I should've listened to the other 1 star helpers when they said it was hard to get into contact with anyone at the spa, but of course I had Lauryns personal number and she always used to get back to me, until shit started to hit the fan with her spa. I did a 5 star review for Lauryn because she asked me to, because she was going through legal shit with the spa and and her ex partner. Lauryn took $225 for a package of 3 massages and didn't refund me when I asked about it. She said she would have her travel table and travel to me and give me my massages but when I text her, she always has an excuse. Hopefully she's using our money for something good."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2016-10-17 21:15:54', 'review_text': 'I had been coming here for a while and really enjoyed it. I purchased a 4 massage package for $200ish and then when I next called for my appointment, I found out it was closed. 

They never called me to let me know and they did not try to refund me.'}]}

{'name': 'Santa Ynez Burrito', 'address': '956 Embarcadero Del Norte Hwy', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Mexican', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-23:0', 'Friday': '11:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-06-07 00:01:08', 'review_text': 'Their 5$ Breakfast Burritos are my staple. Super filling, enough for 2 meals. I love their green salsa, its just enough spicy to make you sweat but enough flavor for you to keep adding it to your food.

The owner is really sweet! and the ambience is nice. A great place to check out!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-05-28 20:01:08', 'review_text': "Service was excellent and really clean location. The food was delicious; had the chimichanga and burrito. Trust me, it's worth it :)"}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2016-05-15 07:49:55', 'review_text': "My first time here, I got a chicken burrito with the works. Delicious. I enjoyed it than all the other burritos in IV. The chicken was flavorful, everything was warm. It hit the craving spot. 

Second time, ended up getting a steak burrito with the works. Not for me. Steak was chewy and made the burrito less enjoyable. Haven't been back since but I will give it one more chance when I get a burrito craving (but I haven't craved a burrito since)."}]}

{'name': 'Trattoria Vittoria', 'address': '30 E Victoria St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Italian, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '17:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '17:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '17:0-21:0', 'Friday': '17:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '17:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '17:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': None, 'street': True, 'lot': False, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': None, 'divey': False, 'intimate': None, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': None, 'casual': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 04:55:39', 'review_text': "Great italian food. came here on a whim and thorough enjoyed it. will return next time i'm visiting santa barbara."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-11 08:50:25', 'review_text': "Their homemade pasta dishes, lasagna, tortellini and ravioli with a heavenly tomato sauce was definitely one of the most delicious dishes I've tried (and then I've been to Italy). The servers where so funny and genuine, too. We'll be back in SB when we get the chance!"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-08 17:23:35', 'review_text': 'We had an early dinner here. It filled up fast so if you can make reservations you should. 

We had an awesome dinner. Atmosphere was perfect.  Wine was delicious and the service was great. 

Next time I will come early and have a drink at the bar. Looked like a fun crowd. Enjoy!'}]}

{'name': 'August Ridge Vineyards', 'address': '5 E Figueroa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Wineries, Arts & Entertainment, Wine Tasting Room, Wine Bars, Nightlife, Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Wednesday': '12:0-19:0', 'Thursday': '12:0-19:0', 'Friday': '12:0-20:0', 'Saturday': '12:0-20:0', 'Sunday': '12:0-16:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-08-10 02:22:21', 'review_text': 'My wife and I eloped last fall and stopped in for an impromptu wine tasting during that weekend. It was the best tasting experience we have ever had! The service was unparalleled and the wine was absolutely delicious. (The gentleman that helped us was wearing a super cool hummingbird shirt.... Thanks for the tasting!)

I would highly recommend that if you ever find yourself in SB, you make it a point to stop by! I know we will when we make it back! Thanks for giving us one of our favorite memories of the weekend!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-07-18 00:10:26', 'review_text': 'Wow, such a fan! Came here for special event that included a tasting. I really love the Italian varietals offered which is kind of rare for this area since most of the wineries produce Rhône varietals. The winemaker himself shared details about the production of the wine which made it really interactive. I really like whites but they are all really enjoyable. My favorite white was the Pinot Grigio. 

Even as a local of four years, I had never visited any of the businesses in Arcada Plaza. I found out that many businesses there have a deal where they waive the corkage fee if you bring in a bottle from August Ridge, super great info! I would highly recommend this tasting room to friends who want to try out different varietals!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-06-13 02:50:49', 'review_text': 'Looking forward to coming here soon'}]}

{'name': "C'est Cheese", 'address': '827 Santa Barbara St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Specialty Food, Cheese Shops, Cafes, Restaurants, Breakfast & Brunch, Wine Bars, Sandwiches, Food, Event Planning & Services, Caterers, Bars, Nightlife', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '1:0-1:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-12-28 20:43:32', 'review_text': 'I loved this place. It is like a candy store for cheese and cured meats. We came here pre-covid and it was packed. 
We waited our turn and when it was the staff was so nice asking us what we liked and icing us samples of what they had and offering suggestions. Turns out if you get a cheese board, you can have it delivered to the winery next door so that is exactly what we did. We got their standard board which for $25 had three cheese, some bits and some fig jam and added two more selections.  Everything was delicious and the board was presented beautifully. 

The shop also has a bunch of cheese related items like knives as well as other kitchen items like hand towels, glasses and cutting boards. And of course they sell bottles of wine and spreads to go along with the cheese.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-04-09 23:42:25', 'review_text': "Wonderful cheese and snack selection! I ordered a big delivery as part of my quarantine grocery situation, and it is sooo worth it. We got 7 different cheeses, olives, baguette, chicken pate, ham, dolma, arancini, and a bottle of white. Everything is delicious, especially the cheese of course. I asked my husband how the ham is, and his eyes literally rolled back in his head. C'est Cheese - you got that yummy yummy."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-03-24 00:12:29', 'review_text': 'Popped in the other day to get my cheese and charcuterie fix. I went with a classic French Brie and a little of the mole and caprese salamis (both have a nice little kick). I can never resist the fresh baguettes!  Staff are always very knowledgeable and will help you find something that matches your taste it to pair with a particular wine you plan to enjoy. I usually end up sampling a couple new cheeses and am always blown away by the variety. So grateful to have this local gem within walking distance to feed my cheese addictions.'}]}

{'name': 'Reds Bin 211', 'address': '211 Helena Ave', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Bars, Tapas Bars, Restaurants, Pubs, Wine Bars, Nightlife, Coffee & Tea', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '15:0-1:0', 'Wednesday': '15:0-1:0', 'Thursday': '15:0-1:0', 'Friday': '15:0-1:0', 'Saturday': '13:0-1:0', 'Sunday': '13:0-1:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': True, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-04-30 05:17:13', 'review_text': 'Reds Bin is a chill lil spot in Santa Barbara I have come to frequent. If you get sick of the State Street scene and want a bit of a different, more relaxed vibe, I would go to Reds. The bar food is also super yummy, and the bartenders are lovely people. I really love this place.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2016-04-23 01:42:23', 'review_text': 'Not a fan of a place who likes to serve alcohol to underage kids...... Prob should think bout hiring some new bartenders.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-03-29 22:03:46', 'review_text': 'This place was so fun. Great cocktails. Great vibe. 

My boyfriend and I hung out here while we were visiting Santa Barbara on a saturday night. There was ample seating (which is a huge deal to me). 

The bartenders were super great and it seemed like a place for locals. Not touristy which was great.'}]}

{'name': 'Pick Up Stix', 'address': '5701 Calle Real', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Chinese, Restaurants, Fast Food', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-13 20:44:58', 'review_text': "If it has to be fast-food Americanized Chinese, I won't even consider Panda Express. But Pick up Stix is the best you can get in under 5 minutes. While their portion sizes tend to be under-whelming, their ingredients and general tastiness is a good compromise to the pig slop served elsewhere. This particular location is usually pretty clean and generally has friendly staff.

If you are in a hurry, stop by Pick Up Stix for some decent food."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2010-02-22 17:55:02', 'review_text': "Went to this place for the first time the other day.  It's sooo good! For a place that cooks fast, it's way better than panda express!  

Shrimp fried rice and honey chicken was what I got...and you get your moneys worth! and then they have a dollar menu too, hahaha. They have egg rolls on it, wontons, edamame, dumplings!  The food is bomb!"}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2009-09-16 05:27:21', 'review_text': "Kung Pao Chicken w/ Fried Rice for Mom. Pad Thai Chicken & Shrimp for me. $16 dollars, no drinks. Why did I wander away from my normal order? The pad thai was...ehhhh so-so. Kung Pao was pretty good, Rice was gross. Took 15 mins to get the food and no one was in there. I've had it before when I would have given 4 stars. Won't be rushing back."}]}

{'name': 'Skyenna Wine Lounge', 'address': '12 Helena Ave', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Wine Tasting Room, Venues & Event Spaces, Caterers, Event Planning & Services, Arts & Entertainment, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Nightlife, Wine Bars, Food, Wineries, Bars', 'hours': {'Monday': '13:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '13:0-20:0', 'Friday': '13:0-20:0', 'Saturday': '13:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '13:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': None, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': None, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-15 01:24:55', 'review_text': "Located a block from State St. and the Santa Barbara Pier, you'll find a funky little Bohemian wine establishment called Skyenna Wine Lounge. We stopped in at the end of a long day of tastings, so we just shared a 5 pour mixed tasting of 2 whites ('20 Sauvignon Blanc and a '20 Viognier) and 3 reds ('20 Grenache, '19 Tempranillo, and '20 Cab. Sauvignon).

Lenny, Skyenna's winemaker, poured for us and was an amazing host. We sat by ourselves in the far back of the lounge while he had a tasting bar full of people at the other end of the building. That didn't stop him from spending plenty of time with us discussing his wines and our interests. The wines we tasted were light to medium bodied and quite flavorful. If you're hungry or just want to create your own food/wine pairing experience, you can order food from the neighboring Italian restaurant, Lucky Penny.

Definitely worth your time to stop in and experience Skyenna's cool vibe atmosphere and Lenny's wines."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 20:10:43', 'review_text': 'Great place with a great vibe! Would highly recommend this place! The wine is so delicious as well! The owner is so nice and personable. Thank you for a great time!'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-14 08:20:55', 'review_text': "It's a pretty small place but not in a bad way. It has bar seating and lounge seating. The owner was very nice and down to earth. The bathroom is a bit of a hassle being around the back but not to bad. It has some interesting art. It's a nice laid back feel. Walking distance from the water. There's street parking. You can check out a nearby restaurant as well. The wine is good. I got a bottle."}]}

{'name': "Mony's Mexican Food", 'address': '217 E Anacapa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Mexican', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:30-15:30', 'Tuesday': '10:30-15:30', 'Wednesday': '10:30-15:30', 'Thursday': '10:30-15:30', 'Friday': '10:30-15:30', 'Saturday': '10:30-15:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': None, 'romantic': False, 'divey': None, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': None, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-17 22:50:16', 'review_text': 'All four of us had an amazing experience. Guacamole is the thicker rather than creamy. More so a pico de gallo con guacamole. 

Burrito had some great fresh rice and beans! 

Give a try of the mole and mango salsa. We went back for more!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-08 21:08:38', 'review_text': 'The tacos tasted unbelievably good, there was so much flavor in them which was the highlight.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-21 04:00:13', 'review_text': 'Best tacos and salsa bar in SB. Very reasonable too, friendly staff. Avocado salsa is so yummy.'}]}

{'name': 'Dogtown', 'address': '888 Embarcadero Del N', 'city': 'Isla Vista', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Hot Dogs, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-3:0', 'Friday': '11:0-3:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-3:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-28 16:27:59', 'review_text': 'Had a BBQ Burger and Crisscut fries from this location which was very delicious. However, this restaurant is no longer here and is being replaced with The Habit Burger [!!!!].'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-14 00:40:03', 'review_text': 'This is my favorite place in Isla Vista hands down.  Not only are the hotdogs/sausages great but their burgers are surprisingly the cheapest and most delicious in town!  It does not end there, the sweet potatoe fries are AMAZINGLY delicious, affordable and plentiful!'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2012-04-11 03:18:49', 'review_text': "This place was a go-to when I lived in Isla Vista.  I'd always go for hotdog, sourkraut and mustard, simple and delicious. 

What really sets this place a part from your average hot-dog joint are the dogtown fries.  Think of them as Nacho fries.  They are so amazing.  The fries are loaded with beans, guacamole, onions, jalapenos, grated cheese, & bacon bits.  

These alone give them 4/5 stars. The missing star is the price (but really, what isn't over priced in Isla Vista) and for being a hot dog place, I really wish the hot dogs were amazing instead of okay."}]}

{'name': 'Revolver', 'address': '1429 San Andres St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Pizza', 'hours': {'Wednesday': '16:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '16:0-22:0', 'Friday': '16:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '16:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '16:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'divey': True, 'hipster': None, 'casual': None, 'touristy': None, 'trendy': True, 'intimate': None, 'romantic': None, 'classy': None, 'upscale': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-06 20:15:13', 'review_text': "Nothing derails my good intentions of starting a diet like a Revolver Pizza craving! It's absolutely the BEST!! Beautifully handmade crust and fresh toppings. Not fancy just delicious. And the salads are incredible. Best Caesar with real anchovy dressing. Market salad has yummy dill ranch, shaved vegetables on yummy lettuce. I don't love the atmosphere, so we always get it to go. It's super popular so get your order in early! But it's definitely our favorite pizza in SB."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-01 06:13:46', 'review_text': 'Great pizza but limited toppings odd hours and long wait time for food.

They really should open at 11am like any other normal pizza place.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-20 02:58:37', 'review_text': "Hands down the best dang pizza in all of Santa Barbara. Not even close. Simple menu and from the crisp on the crust and bottom to the tang in the red sauce, SB you have a winner. It's artisan pizza meets NY on the west coast. Proves you don't need to be in the funk zone to have something great and feels like Brooklyn back 20
Years ago in the fact that they are hip but hard working and making something great. The Caesar salad had a great dressing and fresh greens to boot."}]}

{'name': 'The French Table', 'address': '129 E Anapamu St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Gastropubs, French, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-22:0', 'Friday': '11:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '8:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': True, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2014-05-12 15:42:30', 'review_text': "THE FRENCH TABLE is no longer in business but there is a new restaurant in it's place called PIANO GASTROLOUNGE.  Great food, great service and the same incredible view.  If you were a fan of The French Table than you should definately come by and try this new menu.  The brunch was very good,  I had a simple soprano omelete which turned out to be not so simple.  It was delicious.  I think it was the carmelized onions that did the trick and made it so unique.  Sit ouside if you can, it is so quiet, beautiful and relaxing."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2014-03-18 00:09:27', 'review_text': 'This place totally came out of nowhere and it is adorable! 

My server named Dustin was incredibly attentive and kind. 

Plus this world needs more creperies, and The French Table excels in that arena.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2014-02-21 04:47:01', 'review_text': "It's sad to saw but the food was really good but the service was horrid. Working in the food industry I was shocked. My friend and I were ignored by the first waiter who was flirting with a group of girls so we went to the bar. The bartender was busy talking with off the clock staff drinking for free. We were basically ignored. She also made up an excuse not to use our living social deal. Won't be going back. Staff was a joke."}]}

{'name': 'Paradise Store & Grill', 'address': '1 Paradise Rd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'American (Traditional), Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '9:0-18:0', 'Tuesday': '9:0-18:0', 'Wednesday': '9:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '9:0-18:0', 'Friday': '9:0-19:0', 'Saturday': '9:0-19:0', 'Sunday': '9:0-18:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2016-04-03 23:33:30', 'review_text': "Oh no!  They're closed for good!  Must have just happened.  A shame. This was a great place to stop after a hike in the Paradise Road area."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-03-30 19:02:09', 'review_text': "Neat, historic general store...and so much more!  Rustic little stop, seating on front deck, or out back nestled in the trees.  Both have live music usually!  Not a rock band, but one guy, one guitar, one voice.  So enjoyable for 20 minutes, or the entire afternoon!

Two words: Tritip Chili.  So good.  Even if all you do is stop for a couple of containers of the stuff (don't forget onions and cheese) and take them home.  You won't regret it.  Used to do that on the way home EVERY camping trip we made to Rancho Oso.  But don't be fooled, this place may have the best burger in SB County.  EVERYTHING on the menu is fantastic...and even a little better due to ambiance.

Don't sell yourself short.  Stop here at the Paradise Store."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2015-12-01 21:08:21', 'review_text': 'Nice people. Did not try the food.the rating is for the 10$ they charged for a very small box of firewood.'}]}

{'name': 'Piranha Restaurant & Sushi Bar', 'address': '714 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Sushi Bars', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-08-08 19:51:46', 'review_text': 'The sushi was mediocre but I still like the environment and the service!'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2008-07-26 05:03:21', 'review_text': '"after a lovely day at the beach, my husband and i decided to finish off the day with some sushi. we'd eaten at piranha before and enjoyed it, but after tonight's experience, i can safely say we will never return. it wasn't heinous--but for 80$, the quality of the food and service was pretty abysmal. not only was the sushi NOT super fresh and tasty, especially as compared to katsuya in encino, but the waitstaff was inattentive (we had to call out for the hostess finally to get our waitress's attention), the waitress made a mistake on our order and did not recitfy it (she brought out sea urchin instead of eel--when we brought it to her attention, she did not remove the unwanted, uneaten item from our bill), AND there was a long hair in one of our rolls! At most sushi establishments, they bring out the items as they are prepared, but here, we had to wait a fairly long time before  being served, and then it was everything, all at once.  Plus, i really like it when the meal commences with a nice, warm hand towel and some complimentary edaname--typical of most sushi places, but NOT here. Overall, a very unpleasant, unappetizing, unsatisfying gastronomical experience!"'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-06-02 15:01:40', 'review_text': "This is a nice place to sit outside on State St.  I was a tad bit early for sushi (they don't start making sushi until 5:30), so I decided on their Warm Spinach Salad instead.  It was deeeelish.  I had a blackberry martini to sip on, which was also really good.  The server was really nice and attentive the entire time.  

I've also been here previously and have sat in their outside area upstairs, which is also nice.  

I'm curious to try their sushi soon, which might alter my rating."}]}

{'name': "Sam's To Go", 'address': '315 Meigs Rd, Ste I', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Restaurants, American (New)', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-21:0', 'Friday': '10:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-19:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-03 00:05:08', 'review_text': "This was our first time at Sams and it was delicious!! Excellent customer service, they were so sweet. We got the #11 Italian cold cuts, and the veggie sandwich #29 both were so good! The bread was so fresh and you could tell the ingredients were really quality! My daughter got the turkey sandwich and she is the pickiest eater and she loved it! Can't wait to go back"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-10 03:34:00', 'review_text': "The couple who runs the place are so nice and funny, and the sandwiches are delicious. It doesn't look fancy, but do yourself a favor and try it out. The Pastrami Avocado and Cheese was delicious. Warning, the medium size sandwich is BIG."}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-28 21:43:45', 'review_text': 'I've been going to Sam's for the past several years while visiting beautiful Santa Barbara from the San Francisco Bay area. I've always enjoyed the sandwiches from Sam's. Unfortunately, my wife and I just finished eating their turkey sandwich and in all honesty, it' was just, Ok, more like disappointing...

We were disappointed because it appears the quality and taste of the sandwich has digressed to a "point of no return"... The sandwich was sloppily made, poorly wrapped, and importantly, the man behind the counter (usual guy) seems to have gotten cantankerous over time. He chastised me for not ordering both white and wheat bread sandwiches the way he wanted, getting perturbed for asking for olives in my sandwich and, he had a smart alec - bad attitude demeanor about him - poor customer service.

Suffice it to say, we will not be going back to Sam's. There are too many good delis in the Cliffs Dr. area to be subjected to poor quality sandwiches and an unpleasant customer experience...'}]}

{'name': "Basil's Italian", 'address': '608 Anacapa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Delis, Pizza, Italian, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-21:0', 'Friday': '11:0-21:30', 'Saturday': '11:0-21:30', 'Sunday': '16:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': True, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2018-10-22 02:03:20', 'review_text': 'Went tonight to find the place closed  - looks like for good. Everything was gone but tables and chairs. Sad - it became our go to Italian place.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-10-06 03:20:21', 'review_text': "This place is amazing. If you want great authentic Italian and warm friendly service... this is where you need to be. It blows my mind more people don't know how good this place is. Top 3 Italian in town for sure: the complimentary bread is amazing. The wine... delicious and my tummy is never unhappy leaving here. JUST COME!! You will not regret it :) love you basil's!!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-09-28 21:22:14', 'review_text': 'Off the beaten path but well worth a visit!

Had lunch here today. The sweet server brought out some soft foccacia bread. Combo pizza was hot and loaded with fresh toppings. Egg plant parmesan was Panko breaded and topped with a rich tomato sauce with delicious pasta on the side. 

Shout out to Rosemary...thank you!'}]}

{'name': 'On the Side', 'address': '6521 Pardall Rd', 'city': 'Isla Vista', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'American (Traditional), Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2010-08-04 21:32:49', 'review_text': "Meh.

Granted, as a vegetarian I may not be the intended diner of OTS. That being said, I've been a couple times with different omnivorous friends who have ranging impressions of the place. While some of my friends seem to like it, many seemed underwhelmed by the wings, their staple item. I've gotten the artichoke hearts a couple times, which are decent, but offensively overpriced. This seems to be the moral of On the Side's story.

Possibly the place's saving grace is their great selection of brews. Unfortunately, their selection comes with a price. They have a bunch of flat screens, so I'd say this is a good place to grab a drink and watch a game, but I wouldn't recommend it much further than that."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2010-07-15 17:47:10', 'review_text': 'They changed the way you order which is TOTAL CRAP!!! Instead of resteraunt style ordering everyone has to order up at the counter now which is just ridiculous. They need to change this back again ASAP!'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2010-06-24 00:21:25', 'review_text': 'Good food. The portions looked kinda small at first, but was full by the time I finished everything. My favorite item is the buffalo wings, they might be some of the best in santa barbara. The service was like whatevers, the waitress was kind of a noob and forgot about taking back the bill so i had to go up to the counter and pay there.'}]}

{'name': 'Mika', 'address': '7020 Market Place Dr', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Japanese', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 2.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-31 03:46:28', 'review_text': "Had the Ai Roll Ai Roll, not very good... I mean it's edible and tastes okay.. but I don't think it justifies the price."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-25 19:38:36', 'review_text': "Chicken bowl was disappointing. When I asked for white meat only they informed me that they only carry dark meat.... 

I consider myself to be pretty easy to please,considering my college budget, however I'm pretty sure I will never eat there again...unless forced.


I will not be returning, no matter what they change the name too."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-11 15:30:57', 'review_text': "So I came with a group of co-workers after tring to figure out a place to eat. I was craving something somewhat healthy so I went with the Teriyaki chicken bowl. I asked for brown rice but they only serve white. the chicken tasted rubbery and they loaded they soaked the bowl with sauce. Even though it was only $6 bucks I wouldn't have spent a $1 on this! The service was extra slow and the staff wasn't friendly. I will not be back."}]}

{'name': 'Char West', 'address': '221 Stearns Wharf', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Fish & Chips, Food, Seafood, American (Traditional), Fast Food, Coffee & Tea, Breakfast & Brunch', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-17:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-17:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-17:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-17:0', 'Friday': '7:0-17:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-19:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-19:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': True, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': True, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-26 04:52:35', 'review_text': "It was the worst fish n chips I've ever had. I believe the fish was tilapia as it tasted muddy. We felt disgusted after eating there. The same type of fish was used in the fish taco. We were hungry and was super disappointed with the meal. If you want to eat muddy tasty fish, you can give it a try. It's worst than the frozen fish from the grocery store."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-09 18:16:50', 'review_text': "Nice stop on the pier for coffee

This is a no frills, no fuss, coffee shop (but also serves  food?!) right on the edge of the pier.  It looks like they are not getting extremely high marks for food, but if you go into the place it doesn't feel like a spot for a gourmet meal. What it is great for, and why I'm giving it four stars, is because of the beautiful view over the pier.  It has some awesome seating on the rail, right outside. I suggest going there early in the morning, maybe even for sunrise, and getting a coffee. I also grabbed a bagel, toasted with cream cheese. It felt like a Bagel experience you would have at Starbucks or coffee bean. 

Stop in for the coffee and the views!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-17 17:55:00', 'review_text': 'Absolutely my favorite spot for breakfast in Santa Barbara! Casual outdoor dining area on Stearns wharf with absolutely gorgeous view of the ocean and the hills of Santa Barbara. Francisco, Blanca and the rest of the staff are always friendly and offer excellent service. They serve a range of espresso drinks, and a nice breakfast (and lunch) menu. My personal favorite is the huevos rancheros.  A great place to eat and appreciate the beauty of Santa Barbara.'}]}

{'name': 'State & A Bar and Grill', 'address': '1201 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Restaurants, Nightlife, Barbeque', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-07-17 01:38:31', 'review_text': 'Flashback!  My old happy hour spot. Great outdoor patio. Glad I got one last visit in. They are closed now and new restaurant is on the way.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-14 14:12:39', 'review_text': 'food was good, maybe a little over priced, but what they lacked in quality they made up for in customer service.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2011-04-13 11:15:00', 'review_text': "I seriously thought I was on candid camera or something.  I came in for a late lunch one day and everything I got here was absolutely wretched...even their drinks!

Its such a shame because they have a great location and a nice outdoor patio...how do they stay in business??

I must say this place also gets an award: the absolute worst calamari I've ever sampled in my life (and that's saying something)."}]}

{'name': 'Nikka Ramen', 'address': '5701 Calle Real', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Japanese, Ramen', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '17:0-21:30', 'Wednesday': '17:0-21:30', 'Thursday': '17:0-21:30', 'Friday': '17:0-21:30', 'Saturday': '17:0-21:30', 'Sunday': '17:0-21:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': None, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': True, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-19 06:15:16', 'review_text': "Amazing place, great food , great location. The atmosphere was fun, the music was great. I can tell it's a very popular spot. Servers are very attentive. I will definitely go back again."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-18 01:53:38', 'review_text': "Officially my favorite ramen spot. We don't live in the area but now make it a point to stop by and satisfy our Nikka craving whenever we're in Goleta.

The gyoza was a yummy appetizer but the spicy tuna was sooooo goood! I could eat 10 of those! The basic pork tonkatsu was just as delicious as I remember. Al dente noodles and broth cooked to perfection. The pork chashu is A1 quality. Every ingredient was meant to be on that plate from the tender pork chunks to the salad to the soft boiled egg.

We love Nikka. Period."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-07 01:34:51', 'review_text': 'Holly F@ck... mind blowing. Literally spent the last 20 minutes of my life having a mouth gasm. My knees are weak, And ima little sweaty. This ramen just had its way with me.... and I liked it'}]}

{'name': "Rodney's Grill", 'address': '633 E Cabrillo Blvd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Hotels, Restaurants, Steakhouses, Hotels & Travel, Seafood, Nightlife, Event Planning & Services, Wine Bars', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '17:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '17:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '17:0-22:0', 'Friday': '17:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '17:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'paid', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-11-24 18:54:58', 'review_text': "Amazing dinner at Rodney's Grill.  The foie gras was the best I've ever eaten! And the steak with chantrells was heavenly!  Kudos to this new chef, Chef Moissin!!!  Thanks for making our Thanksgiving dinner so awesome!  Our waitress from Montenegro was super nice also!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-11-23 02:15:24', 'review_text': "I know the chef is new and that the Hilton just took over this location, but we had our Thanksgiving dinner there today, and it felt like they had always been there. From the greeting at the door, to the service, the cocktails, the meals, it was excellent. Can't wait to go back for dinner on a non holiday. FYI the picky eater ate every single bit of his Turkey dinner... the lobster risotto was flawless with the fish course."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2017-11-11 03:48:11', 'review_text': 'I got the Pecan crusted halibut and it was amazingly scrumptious delicious awesomeness.   Whatever the buttery sauce was that comes with it literally made fireworks go off inside of me when I ate it.  

My wife had the Kansas City strip steak and it also was really good.  Her sauce was a red wine reduction and it was also incredible.  

We had the Parker station Pino Noir red wine and it was smooth and delicious.'}]}

{'name': 'JJ’s Diner', 'address': '413 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Diners, Restaurants, Breakfast & Brunch', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '7:30-13:30', 'Wednesday': '7:30-13:30', 'Thursday': '7:30-13:30', 'Friday': '7:30-13:30', 'Saturday': '7:30-14:0', 'Sunday': '8:0-14:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': False, 'street': False, 'lot': True, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'divey': None, 'hipster': None, 'casual': None, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': None, 'intimate': None, 'romantic': None, 'classy': False, 'upscale': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-30 20:27:18', 'review_text': 'My husband and I were looking for a breakfast place while staying in Santa Barbara. We walked by this place and decided to try it out. First we were greeted with kind smiles and did not have to wait to be seated. Michael was our server and he was so so so kind! We ordered the Chile Verde Omelette and Eggs with Bacon. We received our food fast! The food was great, the service was amazing, and the environment was great!

Give this place a try!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-29 01:04:47', 'review_text': 'Great breakfast and service. Highly recommend. Staff even took care of noisy transients as they came on by - thank goodness !'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-28 19:02:22', 'review_text': "The wait to be seated was short despite the long line, they work quickly to get your food in front of you. The Customer service at this place is awesome and deserves 5 stars by itself. They are very friendly, prompt, and kept our coffees filled. If you notice the other reviews where Karens were complaining about bad service, were leaving reviews around when covid peaked so don't pay attention to those. I assure you the service is great.

The food is not bad, however it is basic, and safe. Don't get me wrong,  the food tasted fine, it's just that they play it safe which I guess is a good thing so that Karens in SB (There are plenty in this town) don't complain."}]}

{'name': 'Left At Albuquerque', 'address': '700 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Tex-Mex, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2010-01-13 20:29:31', 'review_text': 'Was here visiting from out of town. Stayed for most of happy hour a couple days. killer margaritas. And huge selection of tequilas too. 

The reason I gave it a great review is they had an appetizer I have never been able to find anywhere else. It was called "Ball of Fire" "For people that like really hot or just plain lunatics" It was a Habanero Popper. Like a jalapeno popper but WAYYYYY hotter. It was fun trying to cool off with more beer or margaritas. Thank God we had a ride back home. Anyhow great memory & we really enjoyed the chips and salsa & the happy hours.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2009-10-05 21:23:14', 'review_text': 'It was all wrong from the moment I asked if we could sit at the bar to have an appetizer and drinks, and the girl that was seating us said, "yes," but we must order an appetizer.  Then she proceeded to take us out to the patio which confused me because I asked for the bar, but I dismissed that.  She sat us at a table, and we ordered our appetizer and drinks from the server.  He comes back with our drinks and explains that they may ask us to move inside because the patio is reserved for customers ordering dinners rather than just appetizers and drinks.  The patio was not full at all, and we told him we were told that we could order an appetizer alone, but still he said we may have to move later as that is the rule.  No apologies at all.  Ugh - I wanted to leave right after his comment...but I figured I should have my beer first.   First, we never asked to be seated outside; second, if that is a rule at the restaurant, why did they seat us outside when we specifically asked for the bar and told the seater that we were only ordering appetizer and drinks?  

Oh, the appetizer was not so great, but we didn't order anything fancy.  It's possible their other food is really good though.  The server spilled my beer on my sunglasses :( .  We quickly had our drinks and appetizer, paid, then got out of there.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2009-09-23 21:14:27', 'review_text': 'Great outdoor patio area.  Loved the ambiance.  The chips and salsa are good, food was okay.  Nothing special.'}]}

{'name': 'Campus Point Coffee', 'address': '6560 Pardall Rd', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Cafes, Coffee & Tea, Bakeries, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-10 17:12:03', 'review_text': "A friend got me interested in this coffee shop when she mentioned they sell vegan cookies. I'm vegan, and it's actually rather tough to find vegan sweet snacks in IV, so I was excited to try Campus Point. Funnily enough, when I headed over for a studying session, they were sold out! Guess those cookies must be good. 

However, the coconut charcoal mocha I tried was delicious--and vegan! Staff were super friendly, and I appreciated the indoor and outdoor seating options. Also, there's a toilet, which is a bonus, and the empanadas looked really yummy. I'll have to try one next time I visit."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-08 22:10:42', 'review_text': 'Finally a place in Isla Vista with a bathroom!

Beyond the much needed bathroom this cafe offers a plethora of interesting drinks on top of providing all the basics. I got an iced charcoal mocha that was perfect to get rid of my mid afternoon slump.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-08 06:06:23', 'review_text': "This is such a cute lil coffee shop in the heart of IV. There's tables inside and outside to do work or chill, and sometimes there's an open mic outside. Prices are average for your local non-corporate coffee shop. The menu has a wide variety of drinks, and sometimes they post about BOGO's or 50% off on their instagram page. I'd definitely recommend this place to anyone who loves coffee and needs a place to study!"}]}

{'name': 'Kogilicious', 'address': '956 Embarcadero Del Norte', 'city': 'Isla Vista', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Korean, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-23:0', 'Friday': '10:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-12-31 04:01:57', 'review_text': "Half and half beef ribs and pork FTW.  Best I've *ever* had, and I've had a lot of good Korean food."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-08-31 01:14:22', 'review_text': "So. Good. So good. A Kogilicious spicy chicken burrito is one of my favorite foods in the world. But all of the proteins are fantastic- beef, spicy pork, tofu; can't go wrong. Taco, burrito, both are great. And so reasonably priced! Pay cash; you'll get a giant burrito for less than $7, which is unheard of elsewhere in IV. This town desperately needs a proper Korean restaurant, but in the meantime, Kogilicious hits the spot."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2015-07-22 23:44:51', 'review_text': 'Three words, Spicy Pork Burrito.

Bomb.

Bring cash, they charge more if you use a card.'}]}

{'name': 'Fiesta Market & Deli', 'address': '4502 Carpinteria Ave', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Mexican, Restaurants, Grocery, Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-23:0', 'Friday': '7:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-17 20:13:50', 'review_text': "Best burritos in town! Excellent customer service. If they don't carry it they will to try to order it for you."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-17 22:10:44', 'review_text': 'We stopped here with our fifth-wheel trailer. We parked a few blocks up the street.

The food was freshly made and delicious. We tried the Machaca burrito and the chicken fajitas. Best Mexican ever in Carpenteria! 

The market also stocks a huge selection of beer and wine. The cherry on top was finding our favorite Mexican beer that is difficult to find in LA.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-07-25 03:55:43', 'review_text': 'Woww my friend recommended lunch from this place and honestly it just might be my new favorite spot in town! We shared nachos and a torta and the torta was literally the same size as a Costco chicken bake. I was literally expecting it to be half of that size. My order came out to $21 and this could have easily fed 3 people, so you definitely get your moneys worth! Wait time might take about 15-20 minutes since they are always super busy!'}]}

{'name': 'California Wood-Fired Catering', 'address': '', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food Trucks, Event Planning & Services, Pizza, Restaurants, Caterers, Food', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-05-24 00:32:27', 'review_text': 'We had them provide pizza for about 100 folks at Municipal Wine. Food was great -- salad, pizza, and gelato. All great. 

They warned us that it would be hard to get pizzas out for that large a crowd, and they were right. But they did the best they could in the situation and everyone was happy. Their chefs worked hard to please and did a great job. 

Only negatives were: underestimated salad, so we ran out a little early. And Email response was a little slow. That said, a pleasure to work with and tasty food!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2013-07-25 22:35:25', 'review_text': 'California Wood-Fired Catering is delicious and perfect for a casual, fun event! I have had the pleasure of working with them many times for events at the private event venue that I manage. While I have heard from a few clients that the owner can be sometimes difficult to get a hold of, I myself have never had a problem reaching him by calling the number listed on their website. Either way they always come through with the events that they book and the guests always rave about how fun it is having a wood-fired burning oven popping out fresh pizzas as well as how delicious the food is.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2013-07-06 04:21:37', 'review_text': 'This year for 4th of July we checked out the Stow House old fashioned 4th of July:) What a pleasant surprise. We were lucky enough to stumble on these pizza people who were making pizza in special oven:) it was really good and hope they can come to our school carnivals next year:)'}]}

{'name': 'Minnow Cafe', 'address': '9 Breakwater', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Delis', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-11 16:25:16', 'review_text': 'This place is perfect to get some seafood in Santa Barbara! I was glad to be able to find this hole in a wall while walking with my group for lunch. 

I ordered the clam chowder bread bowl and fish and chips. Clam chowder was very delicious and fresh. The fish was crispy and made into perfection. 

The best part is that you can order the food right away and simply sit at the tables outside to eat near the harbor where the ocean is so close. So if you want to get food in a quickly manner in order to have more time to explore the other areas in Santa Barbara, I would highly recommend Minnow Cafe.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-04-08 00:39:53', 'review_text': 'Hard to beat for a fast-food-type breakfast or lunch at the marina. Simple, good food, well prepared.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2011-03-20 03:51:33', 'review_text': "I really like the Minnow...I mean you can't beat the location for a fast food establishment and the Fish Tacos are pretty good...BUT I'm always horrified to discover how much this fast food experience costs.  I mean, it's really not very good food unless you view it as cheap (but it's not).  Great thing, sitting outside by the harbor watching the BPs go by while you eat cheap (seeming) food.  Bad part, greasy spoon food served on paper plates by snarky staff with condiments that blow away...but it ain't cheap.  Guess that's Santa Barbara."}]}

{'name': "Giovanni's", 'address': '1187 Coast Village Rd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Pizza, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2019-01-08 15:17:24', 'review_text': 'Delicious! I go once a week for the lunch special, slice (which is large) and a salad. Service is quick'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-12-02 22:16:29', 'review_text': 'The pizza here is so yummy!
Everyone who worked here was very friendly and accommodating. We got the lunch special and itnwas a good deal. Pizza crust was perfect, just the right thickness soft and chewy, while still holding up. Seasoned with oregano, just the right amount of sauce too.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2018-09-01 04:35:00', 'review_text': "Jesus Christ! Where's the customer service! I don't want to be treated like royalty but I at least want to be acknowledged by employees. If I wanted to be referred to as a fat ass I would have rather it be said to my face...


Ps food sucked."}]}

{'name': 'Pearl Social Santa Barbara', 'address': '131 Anacapa St, Ste B', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Cocktail Bars, American (Traditional), Restaurants, Nightlife', 'hours': {'Monday': '17:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '17:0-19:0', 'Thursday': '17:0-20:0', 'Friday': '17:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '17:30-0:0', 'Sunday': '17:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': True, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 20:19:14', 'review_text': "After a fun tour of the SB Funk Zone, and a delicious meal at The Lark, we all ventured next door to Pearl Social and were happily seated in their lounge are. Such an enchanting space, and perfect for socializing amongst the beautiful people of Santa Barbara.

Thank you Shannon and Alberto for taking such good care of us all. Shannon's drink recommendations were spot-on for all of us. 

Definitely our new favorite chill and cocktail place in the Funk Zone. And thoroughly enjoyed the fun music selections."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 00:58:46', 'review_text': 'Such a fun idea. We really hope they do another. It was a great way to celebrate New Years Day!'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-03 03:51:21', 'review_text': "we stumbled upon this on christmas eve and the vibes were PERFECT!!! super decked out pop up which was great, next christmas go check it out!! the bartenders were so fun and friendly, only reason not giving a 5 is because all the drinks were definitely on the super sweet side (which is fine for those who like it and it's christmas themed anyway so why not indulge?) but not everyone likes that sweet an some of us ending up getting just a beer (guess who) but so so fun!!"}]}

{'name': 'Spiritland Bistro', 'address': '230 E Victoria St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Vegetarian, French, Vegan, Seafood, Asian Fusion, Gluten-Free, American (New)', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '17:30-21:0', 'Wednesday': '17:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '17:30-21:0', 'Friday': '17:30-22:0', 'Saturday': '17:30-22:0', 'Sunday': '17:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2012-08-02 01:04:35', 'review_text': "im very honest with these reviews- look at my other ones. i'm not going to make excuses for places but im also not going to forget to appreciate the little things... and this was one of the best vegan meals i have ever had... EVER had... they are not even entirely vegan which is the shocker- as most non vegan places believe a plate full of vegetables is what us vegans eat.. this place was truly imaginative, and provided me with a perfect four course meal..  yes, i, Shirley, said perfect... a rare thing indeed.
i really wanted to have this place cater my wedding, the second i realized every bite i had was magical, i was truly obsessed with the idea of them catering my wedding- and now that i'm planning it... they're gone. so sad.

wish places like this stayed open.... this and pure luck in silverlake... COME BACK PLEASE!"}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-03-01 05:20:25', 'review_text': 'we'd been wanting to try this place for awhile... but when we finally did - underwhelmed.  the ambience would not have been so bad were there some music or lower lighting, but couldn't help but think, "i'm in a small room with 20 other people we don't know".  the food itself was ok, but not a special night out.  for $10 bucks a plate i would have gone back, but for $20 i'll go elsewhere.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-12-31 16:54:19', 'review_text': 'I called to make reservations for new years eve- this place is closed until further notice FYI. Not sure when they are planning to re-open.'}]}

{'name': "TonyRay's Restaurant & Cantina", 'address': '731 De La Guerra Plz', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Nightlife, Restaurants, Mexican, Dance Clubs', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2014-04-14 16:30:03', 'review_text': "Been to Tony Ray's for the occasional party.   DJ Fab or bunch of drunk Harley dudes, certainly a Fiesta or two.  

As many times as I have been there, I don't really know what it is?   Is it a restaurant?  Does it keep regular hours?   Is it a bar?  Do people go there and hang out on a Thursday night?   The bartenders have always been nice and the drinks have been good.  Not sure if they have glass because it seems that I am always served in a plastic cup.   I know I have eaten the food but I have zero recollection as to whether or not I enjoyed it, it is that forgettable.  

I gave them two stars but I might go back and see if they deserve and upgrade."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2014-03-02 15:38:33', 'review_text': "This is a great spot for a drink and some dessert. The dinner menu is decent but the price and size do not match. Don't come hungry, but do enjoy a specialty drink."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-29 21:40:05', 'review_text': 'my daughters and friends love to go there for karaoke :) so fun! The owners and staff are very sweet!'}]}

{'name': 'Savoy Cafe & Deli', 'address': '24 W Figueroa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Delis, Coffee & Tea, Breakfast & Brunch, Food, Gluten-Free, Cafes, Beer, Wine & Spirits', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:30-16:0', 'Tuesday': '7:30-16:0', 'Wednesday': '7:30-16:0', 'Thursday': '7:30-16:0', 'Friday': '7:30-16:0', 'Saturday': '7:30-16:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-12 18:13:50', 'review_text': 'So good, that we went for breakfast and then again for lunch.

We really loved the gluten-free bread options. I have not had a sandwich in a long time.  It was so thick with turkey!

A very lovely restaurant with a salad bar (yes, really), open space, nice outdoor seating, and a comfortable bar area.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-28 21:02:56', 'review_text': 'Savoy is impeccable.  Somehow every single item is delicious and fresh.  I always have a good experience.  The salad bar is for sure the best in the city.  The sandwiches, excellent.  The entrees, you guessed it, so good.  I would recommend them to anyone -- you gotta try it.  Note: closed Sundays!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-22 20:28:32', 'review_text': "Great food and service! I don't live in the area, but next time I'm in Santa Barbara,  I will definitely eat there."}]}

{'name': 'Brasil Arts Cafe', 'address': '1230 State St, Ste C', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Juice Bars & Smoothies, Breakfast & Brunch, Brazilian, Restaurants, Food, Salad, Acai Bowls', 'hours': {'Monday': '17:0-20:30', 'Thursday': '17:0-20:30', 'Friday': '17:0-20:30', 'Saturday': '10:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-16:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-21 06:50:22', 'review_text': "Our hosts Roberta and Mestre Daniel Yoshimi (aka Prof. Chin) provided an excellent menu of the favorite foods of Brazil (o Brasil, em português). One who appreciates tasty-good food simply cannot stay away very long. My tri tip was delicious, and the multiple traditional sides were exactly on-point. (Prices are friendly too.)

I used to visit this establishment weekly to take part in great African drumming classes, and it's fun to revisit the festive atmosphere and food. They present their cuisine and culture with hospitality, nuance and great cooking skills.

#HighlyRecommended"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-18 05:28:16', 'review_text': 'my boyfriend and I went here for dinner and it was a nice experience :) we each got a caipirinha to drink which was good and my boyfriend LOVED the stroganoff! My Brazilian cesar was good and the brigadiero which we got to go was AMAZING! I would go back to try more! The lady told us to make ourselves at home which was a sweet sentiment!! The people were very nice :,)'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-15 12:06:28', 'review_text': 'The restaurant facility itself may not look all that elegant and appealing but the service and the food really blows that away. They serve food for each meal of the day but I personally would recommend going for breakfast and trying one of their acai fruit bowls. Slightly on the pricier side but so worth it and you will be healthily full for hours to come! The culture here is also something that is unique and interesting. Great place for family brunch!'}]}

{'name': 'Juice Ranch', 'address': '1187 Coast Village Rd, Ste 5', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Food, Live/Raw Food, Juice Bars & Smoothies, Vegan', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '7:30-17:0', 'Wednesday': '7:30-17:0', 'Thursday': '7:30-17:0', 'Friday': '7:30-17:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-14:0', 'Sunday': '9:0-17:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 15:54:28', 'review_text': 'Went in to place an order. No one working there was wearing a mask. Asked if the people making the food wore masks. The kid said "yeah we have masks." Walked out. They don't care about keeping their customers safe. Should not be in the service business. I've been there before and liked their food but clearly never going back again.

Check out all the other "not recommended" and reported reviews on the same issue that have been hidden for their rating.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-13 03:40:09', 'review_text': 'Good high quality and fresh ingredients just expensive and tiny portions. Never have I ever paid $12 for a bagel with mostly raw ingredients. 

Bowls are literally a jar of chia seeds with the least amount of toppings and flavor ever.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-17 16:44:33', 'review_text': "I like their products but I just had a very unpleasant conversation with one of the employees about masks. None of the employees need to wear masks and the one I spoke to shared that he was not vaccinated. He told me he had had COVID and wasn't afraid of COVID. I am. I've had friends die of this disease. I have friends who work in hospitals and witness the toll it has taken. There is less danger of transmission when people wear masks, so why won't this business take this step to look out doe its customers?"}]}

{'name': "Mama's Bakery & Deli", 'address': '5342 Hollister Ave', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Food, Delis, Bakeries', 'hours': {'Monday': '6:0-16:30', 'Tuesday': '6:0-16:30', 'Wednesday': '6:0-16:30', 'Thursday': '6:0-16:30', 'Friday': '6:0-16:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': False, 'street': True, 'lot': True, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2017-04-14 17:12:21', 'review_text': "Solid Banh Mi sandwiches at a decent price. It's not San Francisco, but it will have to do.it work ld be nice if their bread was crispier and if they had lemongrass pork"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2017-03-24 23:17:39', 'review_text': "Really hard to spot out, but I'm glad I found it! I would've never expected this to be a business that served pho and banh mi if I just drove by it, but I'm glad curiosity got the best of me and I'd like to try this place more often. 

I ordered half a pork banh mi with everything on it and it was reminiscent of the Vietnamese spots in the east bay suburbs. My only complaint is their bread isn't as flaky and it's more soft and dense, but it does the job for a craving. They didn't skimp out on the pork which is good. 

The lady running the counter was really nice and I got my sandwich way faster than I'd expect anywhere else in this area. Worth it!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2017-03-15 18:18:55', 'review_text': "Freshest sandwich in town. The bread is so soft and the ingredients are so fresh. Never greasy, light yet filling. So delicious! My favorite is the pastrami, it's the Wednesday special. If you like your sandwich with everything make sure you let them know or they won't put condiments on it. Must try!"}]}

{'name': "Chad's", 'address': '216 W Cabrillo Blvd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Diners, Salad, American (Traditional), Breakfast & Brunch, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-14:30', 'Tuesday': '7:0-14:30', 'Wednesday': '7:0-14:30', 'Thursday': '7:0-14:30', 'Friday': '7:0-14:30', 'Saturday': '7:0-14:30', 'Sunday': '7:0-14:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': None, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-19 02:02:14', 'review_text': "The absolute BEST eggs benedict (the Californian) that I've ever had.  From the light slightly lemony sauce (not thick and gelatinous) to the soft perfect muffin and am ample perfect amount of spinach ... PERFECT.  JUST PERFECT.

The mimosa flight was stunning as well!

Thanks Chads - we will be back."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 21:30:42', 'review_text': "This place is magical!!!  I would like to give this establishment 10 Stars. We arrived to meet an anticipated Sunday Brunch crowd. The magic begins here! As we waited under the sun blocking covering, we listened to great music over Bose speakers!!! We swayed and enjoyed the day. The owner, Chad, served us delightful muffins and thanked us for coming out then... Mark, the magician, gave us an AWESOME  show!!! Kiri, our waitress, was superior and this place was a WHOLE EXPERIENCE. The food is DELICIOUS!  Visit Chad's! You deserve the best!!!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 19:45:18', 'review_text': "We had breakfast at Chad's this morning and it did not disappoint. We were appreciative and impressed by their attentive service and delicious food. Their complimentary mini muffins to start are so good! We love Chad and everything he brings to our community. Thank you!"}]}

{'name': "Carl's Jr", 'address': '7 S Milpas St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Burgers, Fast Food, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-22:0', 'Friday': '7:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2020-06-11 18:05:33', 'review_text': "The food is what you expect from Carl's Jr.  Tasty but way too salty. 

I think the drink guy might be speaking English but I am not sure. I think he is refusing to give me another drink refill. Not even if I pay for it. I thought I was minding my business after eating lunch. I guess he is too busy with his other duties of standing around the drink machine doing nothing. 

Fortunately, McDonald's is a couple of blocks north and Habit (which is actually pretty good) is a couple of blocks south, so it is not hard to find a place where people want to work."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-14 06:09:11', 'review_text': "This is one of the best Carl's jrs I've been to. The cashier was super friendly and helpful.  The food was good and the restaurant was clean. It has an old time retro vibe. My special request was done without hesitation."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2019-09-03 20:22:37', 'review_text': "its Carl's Jr, what else is there to say. the food either taste good that day or gross. staff friendly, restaurant and facilities something clean."}]}

{'name': "Alphie's Restaurant", 'address': '5725 Hollister Ave', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Burgers, American (Traditional), Breakfast & Brunch, Diners', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '6:0-14:0', 'Wednesday': '6:0-14:0', 'Thursday': '6:0-14:0', 'Friday': '6:0-14:0', 'Saturday': '6:0-14:0', 'Sunday': '6:0-14:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': None, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-03-21 20:01:31', 'review_text': 'Ordered breakfast takeout today for 6 family members.  Everyone was very happy and enjoyed the food.  Thank you for the experience...looking forward to trying lunch items too!'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2020-02-08 19:14:08', 'review_text': "If you want a hardy breakfast at a good price, then this is it! 

I'd go back for the food as it was very good!

Service...not so much."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-11-18 10:50:57', 'review_text': "I'm glad we found this hole-in-the-wall! My friends and I were visiting UCSB from out of town for the weekend and we were looking for a breakfast place before the long trip back home. This place has a cozy atmosphere and I was surprised that there was a live band playing. I ordered the crab omelette and my sister ordered the Loco Moco that they had as one of the day's specials. Both dishes were tasty and hearty, plus reasonably priced. I love how filled the omelette was and how the cheese from inside the omelette would stretch from every forkful! Even the food that my friends ordered looked delicious. The service was also pretty good. Definitely would come again when we come back to visit UCSB."}]}

{'name': 'Rice Garden', 'address': '1180 University Ctr, Bldg 252', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Fast Food, Caterers, Chinese, Szechuan, Event Planning & Services, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-17:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-17:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-17:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-17:0', 'Friday': '10:0-17:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': True, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'paid', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2013-06-08 01:53:14', 'review_text': 'Its a shame, this place used to be so much better last year. They had a much wider variety last year. The curry chicken tasted almost like authentic chinese, and I enjoyed the Spicy Chicken every time. They switched around the menu, but usually they had 2 very good items everyday.

Now, its pretty much the same generic items everyday. On top of that, they are almost always sold out, whether because its rush lunch hour, or its after 2 or 3 and they just give up making half the menu.

I hear its getting replaced by Yoshinoya. I am glad because I love Yoshinoya.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2013-03-07 21:26:31', 'review_text': 'I would say the food was good if I could ever have it. Every time I go to this place they are "out" of what I want, nothing on deck, just simply out. Some times when I go they tell me that things are going to be done at exactly 1pm (which may be over 30 mins away)...its especially frustrating when these should be (and probably are) the money makers for the business. Teriyaki chicken? ITS CHICKEN, why is this not in abundance?? Why does the business run out of it!??! Why is there a 50 cents extra charge for the simplest menu item??! I can't make sense of it, I won't be going back, it is simply absurd.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2012-10-05 21:11:32', 'review_text': "Best place to eat anywhere near UCSB. It's cheap, it tastes awesome, and the service is fast and good. Everything tastes fresh, unlike Panda Express. Too bad it's gone now."}]}

{'name': 'Blenders In the Grass', 'address': '1046 Coast Village Rd, Ste F', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Juice Bars & Smoothies, Food, Restaurants, Vegetarian', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-22:0', 'Friday': '7:0-18:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '8:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': False, 'street': None, 'lot': True, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-09 04:23:38', 'review_text': 'I went to blenders and ordered 2 drinks.  One was a blue pomegranate and it was made short even after using the spatula to pour any excess smoothie into the cup. I know the smoothie is supposed to reach the top of the cup because I used to be a supervisor there. This is not the first time this has happened, it seems to be a reoccurring problem.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-09-21 16:07:13', 'review_text': 'The blenders in montecito last night I go to the register the girl working it goes to it too and just blankly stares at me.

No hello what can I get you no acknowledgment or greeting. I have to initiate my order.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-05-17 20:01:12', 'review_text': 'If you like added sugar in their ice milk and sherbet and non organic gmo tasting fruit and soy milk then this is your place! The fruit juice they add tastes like corn syrup and sugar, maybe 10% real juice.
I dont even think their wheat grass is organic as nothing is labeled organic and non gmo. Hit or miss on customer service and sanitary procedures as it looks as the college kids working their are trying to make them as fast as they can and rarely even blend them long enough, I was loyal but the last straw was when I bought a peanut butter bar and it tasted like moldy peanuts as I looked at the expiration date, it was 3 months expired! The owners have lost touch and the managers are not into customer service. So long...'}]}

{'name': 'Bougainvillea', 'address': '202 State St, Ste A', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Restaurants, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Italian, Pizza', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-10:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-10:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-10:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-10:0', 'Friday': '11:0-10:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-10:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-10:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2009-05-31 00:18:23', 'review_text': 'what a bummer!!! I was so excited to have dinner here and there are huge "for rent" signs in the windows. It will be missed.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2008-08-26 03:30:05', 'review_text': 'My husband and I went here tonight and the food and service was excellent.  He had the deep dish barbecue pizza and I had the ravioli.  The food was delicious.  The service was also very accommodating.  We highly recommend this place.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-05-29 04:33:08', 'review_text': "Atmosphere is very nice here! They have a semi-separate area with a fire place that was great for an anniversary celebration with my girl. Wine list is decent but I felt they didn't offer enough wines by the glass. Food was just good (7 out of 10). She had the Salmon special of the day which was average. I had the Chicken Vesuvio which I really liked. I wanted to try the local wines so I had the Santa Barbara Syrah and she had the S.B. Chardonnay. Both were reasonably priced and well worth it!

Total for the night was $65 for two entrees, two glasses of wine, and Tiramisu (which was excellent).

Highly recommended for a nice place to have dinner. Would've been 5 stars if the food was better."}]}

{'name': "Anna's Marketplace Bakery", 'address': '7018 Marketplace Dr', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Donuts, Restaurants, Bakeries, Food, Sandwiches', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '6:0-17:30', 'Wednesday': '6:0-17:30', 'Thursday': '6:0-16:0', 'Friday': '6:0-17:30', 'Saturday': '6:0-17:30', 'Sunday': '6:0-16:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-18 01:20:49', 'review_text': 'Donuts are delish, nice and light and fresh. The chocolate croissant was really good as well! They are a little more pricey than some donut shops but have really good flavor.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-01 18:44:53', 'review_text': "Happy 2022 everyone! This year will surely see me at Anna's quite a few more times. When a friend told me that a bakery close to where I live offers vegan donuts, I was psyched--I'm vegan and it's oddly difficult to find good vegan food, sweets, and drinks in this area. Checking out Anna's Bakery a few days later, I wasn't let down. 

I've sampled both the vegan glazed donut and the apple fritter, as well as the house coffee, and all were great. The donut is puffy and airy and sweet. The fritter has glorious crunchy, oily edges and a surprisingly doughy interior, complete with apple pieces and a glossy, sugary varnish. (Did you know some 'apple fritters' elsewhere don't even contain apple?) The coffee is hot and black and perfectly balances the candy-like sweetness of the baked goods. 

There's always a long line and seating is limited so be prepared. This shop also offers non-vegan donuts (the majority contain milk products, though I'm crossing my fingers for a vegan cake donut in 2022). There is also a menu of savory food. Breads and donuts and cookies are also available to go. That pink box, unmistakably brimming with tasty treats, is sure to being smiles to any gathering... especially if you have vegan friends who are so used to being left out when sweet baked goods appear."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-27 05:28:12', 'review_text': "SO friendly and donuts are always amazing. All staff, from the cashier to the owner. All lovely people. They always greet with by my name. I love to see how they interact with all customers. I am always happy to give them business as it is very well deserved. Keep up the wonderful work! Anna's has been around for a long time and has always been one of my favorites."}]}

{'name': 'Baba Small Batch', 'address': '103 Sant Felicia Dr', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Restaurants, Mediterranean, Farmers Market, Specialty Food, Organic Stores, Street Vendors', 'hours': {'Monday': '8:0-16:0', 'Tuesday': '8:0-16:0', 'Wednesday': '8:0-16:0', 'Thursday': '8:0-16:0', 'Friday': '8:0-17:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-04-04 19:13:09', 'review_text': "OK, to be honest, I stopped by the Baba stand at the Morro Bay farmers market, not because of the hummus. It was because of the wonderful red-headed gal that was working your booth. She turned out to be charming, helpful and informative. I had never tried hummus before. She explained it to me and helped me choose just the right one. I ended up buying 2 the first week and many more since then. Last week she talked me into trying the bread and I'm glad she did. I love her and I love your product.
Employees like her are hard to find. (I'm really bad with names or I would add it)"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-08-31 07:15:44', 'review_text': "This has to be the best hummus I've ever had and the chips are an added bonus!! They have so many hummus flavors to choose from. Seriously this stuff is compared to drugs. Once you have a taste it, you can't stop. Haha. For the past few years they would make their way up to Fresno's River Park Farmers Market. But sad to say, they didn't come up this year. I'm sure everyone who bought their hummus here in town was saddened when  Baba's hummus didn't make an appearance. I know my family and I were sad. 

I hope I find their hummus when I go to SLO next weekend. If the owner is reading this, please come back to Fresno and sell your amazing hummus!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2017-07-07 05:28:45', 'review_text': "The baba spicy pepper with Harrisa is soooo good! It's a bit spicy so try it before you buy if you can't handle heat. But if you can give it a go. It's amazing."}]}

{'name': 'Aperitivo', 'address': '7 W Haley St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Desserts, Food, Bars, Wine Bars, Coffee & Tea, Nightlife, Tapas/Small Plates, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Wednesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '16:30-21:0', 'Friday': '16:30-21:0', 'Saturday': '16:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 05:03:21', 'review_text': 'I am a foodie, I travel for work and have been fortunate enough to have amazing food all over the world. That being said this is one of the most underrated restaurants in Santa Barbara I can easily say this is one of the top three restaurants in Santa Barbara.  My recommendation would to be to order anything with the burrata on it! The 24 hrs burrata, the pere brushchette , and the stratacciatella brushchette were all amazing! The passion fruit margarita is also to die f

Thank you for upping the food game in Santa Barbara Aperitivo! 

Side note, my other two favorite restaurants in Santa Barbara are the Black Sheep and Bouchon'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-13 02:30:17', 'review_text': "No hesitation here with the 5 star review! Excellent food, stellar service,  and guaranteed high quality product every time.  When I want fresh and delicious pasta, Aperativo is my go-to.  I appreciate their dedication and consistency. Highly recommend for date night since its a cozy intimate venue with an open kitchen. I'm also a big fan of Tues pasta club for take out,  excellent wine pairings every time."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-07 01:01:24', 'review_text': 'I ordered the box of wine for pick up and was not disappointed. They were all wonderful wines! I highly recommend it AND the Pasta Club. The pasta selections are very flavorful and pair wonderfully with the wine. I plan to order everytime I am in town.'}]}

{'name': 'Panino', 'address': '5666 Calle Real', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Delis, Restaurants, Soup, Salad, Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-16:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-16:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-16:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-16:0', 'Friday': '10:0-16:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-16:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-15:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-04-22 19:38:05', 'review_text': "Okay, this was not exactly what I expected, but its a delightful surprise!! I decided to try something new and go with the English Stilton and pear sandwich today...I don't know why, but I assumed the cranberries and walnuts would be in a kind of chutney so when I opened my sandwich I was kind of disappointed until I took a bite. HOLY COW ITS DELICIOUS! Everyone should try this sandwich on Foccacia bread!

Classic faves of mine also include the Turkey and Salami, Cobb Salad Sandwich, and Caprese Sandwich. I've honestly never had anything that I didn't like. Thanks for another delicious lunch today, Panino!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-01-27 23:52:51', 'review_text': 'A couple of months ago my wife and I had to do some business in Goleta. When we were done we asked where we could get a good sandwich. They recommended Panino. It was great!! Today my wife and I were bored from staying at home cause of the pandemic. We decided to take a drive to Goleta and have lunch at Panino. Again, our sandwiches/lunch were great. Very friendly and good service. Take it from us who drive all the way from Oxnard. Highly recommended!!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-12-04 04:09:52', 'review_text': "Depending on my taste buds for the day, Panino has either the best or the 2nd best sandwich in town. That would be the Italian combo on focaccia. Layered with fine meats and cheeses, it's thoughtfully complemented by a delightful basil aioli, lettuce, and thin cut green bell pepper and cucumber. If one maneuvers the meat and cheese correctly, every bite has the most appealing ratio of ingredients you will ever taste in a sandwich. It's like taking a bite out of the Sistine Chapel, or being able to taste the Mona Lisa. If they ever change it, I will seriously write a strongly worded letter to management. 

If I ever were to try any of their other sandwiches, I'm assuming they would also be delicious. The prices are a bit more than average, much as the price of a Lakers ticket costs more than one for the Clippers."}]}

{'name': "Petrini's Restaurant", 'address': '5711 Calle Real', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'American (New), Italian, Restaurants, Pizza', 'hours': {'Monday': '16:30-21:0', 'Tuesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Wednesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '16:30-21:0', 'Friday': '16:30-21:30', 'Saturday': '16:30-21:0', 'Sunday': '16:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-09-02 07:51:10', 'review_text': "I tend not to expect much from food locations in Strip Malls.  While staying in the Santa Barbara area, I just wanted a good piece of Pizza. We stopped here while on a walk and ordered an onion and cheese pizza, small size.  Neither of us could believe how fresh and great it was! The sauce was a good homemade red with Italian spices and fresh tomato flavor. Just enough good cheese.  We stopped in twice after having such great luck.  Tried the salads, pasta and more pizza, garlic bread and wine.  Family owned and run place that's cordial and homey.   This is the kind of place you find in Chicago and New York. Just a little gem with friendly people and really good Italian food!"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2016-08-17 01:35:09', 'review_text': "Well, I tried eating at this Petrini's again, and I'm really sad to report that the food has gotten worse AND more expensive. The Chicken Picatta was drowning in butter, or grease; I'm not sure what that was. The fettuccine Alfredo that came with it was undercooked and had zero taste. We also were served garlic bread that was burned to black. To make things worse, I took the food home because I just could eat it at the restaurant. I was hungry later so I ate it. 
Oh My God.....I couldn't keep it down. I got such a stomach ache from that food. Petrini's , you are a local restaurant and I really try to support local businesses, but you are bad for my health."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2016-07-11 15:51:04', 'review_text': 'I have not been in here for many years, but we stopped in the other night and it was tasty traditional american italian food for a great price. The meat raviolis were very tender and delicious and the sauce was spot on. The spaghetti and meatballs (the yard stick for any italian review) were also very good. I also really enjoyed my cup of minestrone soup, really hit the spot. The waiters were very attentive and the place had a very welcoming and tidy atmosphere. 

The only downside, the water tasted horrible, I think they need to replace their filter or something.'}]}

{'name': 'Haggen Food & Pharmacy', 'address': '175 N Fairview Ave', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Delis, Drugstores, Restaurants, Food, Shopping, Grocery, Bakeries', 'hours': {'Monday': '6:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '6:0-0:0', 'Wednesday': '6:0-0:0', 'Thursday': '6:0-0:0', 'Friday': '6:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '6:0-0:0', 'Sunday': '6:0-0:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 2.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2015-11-02 06:05:33', 'review_text': "Went in after the change from Vons for some whole wheat flour and was surprised that the flour was over $8 for 5 pounds. Next time I went to Smart and final and the King Arthur flour is $3.99 regular price. I live in Goleta so next time I went back to Haggens to compare and they had the King Arthur flour for $6.49 with 20% off which is still $5.15. I have been shopping in the same store since the Safeway opened in the 60's but I am done now with this kind of price increase."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2015-10-26 10:12:53', 'review_text': 'I decided to give this Haggen location a chance. I walked into an mostly empty store. I notice some items that have been marked down in the deli due to product expiring the same day. I take it up to the register. The store manager was at the register. She refused to honor the discount on the packaging and said it was a mistake. Haggen, you can keep your expired food!'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2015-10-22 07:50:28', 'review_text': 'Really? I know you're going out of business Haggen but you expect me to pack my own groceries now? 

Now, even though I am an educated professional on a 6+ figure salary, I am not above stuffing some groceries in a shopping bag. It's obviously not difficult. However, if you want me to do your job for you, you've got to be nice to me. Last time I was in the store the portly middle aged man just threw my groceries onto the conveyer belt and left them to pile up at the end. He never acknowledged my existence except to grunt the total to me. 

You can either pack my damn groceries or I walk out next time. Not sorry you'll soon be out of a job if that's the level of "service" you provide. Pfft.'}]}

{'name': "Rusty's Pizza Parlor", 'address': '111 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Pizza', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-0:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-0:0', 'Friday': '11:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-0:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-0:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': None, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-18 19:14:33', 'review_text': 'Really good pizza, reasonable prices, nice setting, late hours, quick pickup.....'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-06 21:11:26', 'review_text': "Garbage customer service. Owner should just have a self order computer at the counter.Pizza was decent. Don't come here."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-12 01:30:37', 'review_text': "Had a homeless person in here eating, shopping cart and all. Kids are riding around indoors on electric scooters. Staff are unfriendly and unresponsive. Service is slow. 

They must be really underpaid or something because it really seems like no one cares at all here. 

Best part of my visit today was find a finger nail in my salad. I'm a dude, it's a a chick's finger nail. Did they seriously not wear gloves when servicing the salad bar or something? People are probably chewing their finger nails while making my food. Disgusting."}]}

{'name': 'Jeannine’s American Bakery & Restaurant', 'address': '1 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Bakeries, Restaurants, Patisserie/Cake Shop, Cafes, Coffee & Tea', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '7:30-13:30', 'Wednesday': '7:30-13:30', 'Thursday': '7:30-13:30', 'Friday': '7:30-13:30', 'Saturday': '7:30-13:30', 'Sunday': '7:30-13:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': None, 'street': True, 'lot': False, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-19 17:31:21', 'review_text': 'Very nice place for breakfast close to Stearns Wharf. And if you like French toast, try the Kahula Banana! Wow! Amazing. 

Service is excellent! Order at the bakery counter and your order will be served at your table. Indoor and outdoor seating. Good coffee too!

This is the breakfast place!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-19 03:51:07', 'review_text': 'Awesome location and great food. Customer service is top notch   and food comes out quick.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-15 17:48:18', 'review_text': 'I ordered the espresso chocolate chip scone and it was perfect! The breakfast looked delicious. The service was quick and great. Would recommend! Lovely seating looking out to the beach.'}]}

{'name': "Penelope's Sno Balls at the Beach", 'address': '200 Linden Ave', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Food, Hot Dogs, Shaved Ice, Desserts', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-18:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-18:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-18:0', 'Friday': '11:0-17:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-18:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-18:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-13 04:44:03', 'review_text': "Penelope's makes our family beach trips that much better.  We look forward to the shave ice with ice cream and the hotdogs."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-08-22 01:10:07', 'review_text': "Great location on Carpinteria Beach at the end of Linden Avenue.  Penelope is so nice. 

I had the tropical shave ice flavored with Piña colada and blood orange. Yummy.  Perfect on warm days.

There's several benches to sit and people watch.  $3 for a shave ice- great deal.  Large portion you might want to share. For another $1 you can get vanilla ice cream at the bottom.  Enjoy."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-08-20 01:09:41', 'review_text': 'I ordered the Rainbow, which had pineapple and blue raspberry flavor, and it was delicious. I even added ice cream at the bottom which enlightened the whole treat! Very clean and sanitary with a lovely lady running the booth. Also the fact that an International Harvester Scout 2 was pulling the trailer made me enjoy my cold treat by tenfold'}]}

{'name': 'Oakberry Açaí Bowls and Smoothies', 'address': '819-B State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Coffee & Tea, Restaurants, Cafes, Food, Acai Bowls, Juice Bars & Smoothies', 'hours': {'Monday': '8:0-20:0', 'Tuesday': '8:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '8:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '8:0-18:0', 'Friday': '9:0-20:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-20:0', 'Sunday': '8:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-22 19:05:43', 'review_text': "Great Açaí! We stopped here for a quick lunch and it didn't disappoint! Lots of fresh fruit available ans a great variety of toppings. Açaí was a bit thinner than other types I've had but still had great flavor. The chai pudding topping was my favorite - never had that before and it was a nice addition! Would stop by again for sure!"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-19 00:38:41', 'review_text': 'Love this place for a quick lunch or a pick me up! There are plenty of choices for toppings and they have gluten free options. I like adding coconut, peanut butter, bananas, strawberries and granola. My reasoning for the four stars is i feel it is a little overpriced.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-19 03:30:05', 'review_text': '5 star acai bowl, service, and location.  So impressed with this last minute find.  It ended up being a light dinner kinda night for us and with not much open at almost 8pm, but these bowls hit the spot.  

Once you choose the size you want, there is a large list of toppings which are unlimited.  I chose everything that sounded good and I was so impressed with how well they all went together.  My first time having peanut butter with my acai and chai pudding but it messed well.  Fresh, flavorful and filling.  

I know where to stop now when in Santa Barbara.'}]}

{'name': 'De La Vina Lounge', 'address': '2711 De La Vina St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Dive Bars, Bars, Lounges, Nightlife, Pool Halls, Sports Bars', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-2:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-2:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-2:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-2:0', 'Friday': '10:0-2:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-2:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-2:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': True, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-05-18 05:56:58', 'review_text': 'Alice is a saint! Loved finding this gem in Santa Barbara. Enjoy the family vibes when you enter.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-05-12 05:17:30', 'review_text': 'I really hate updating reviews.   First impressions, right??  But in the case of Jimboz, how could I not. I don't want to call myself a regular because honestly I have never been there at 10am for The Price Is Right and never make it more than once in a week.  But I will say I'm a huge fan!  I usually go on Tuesdays which is officially "Ladies Night".  But Alice is always working and treats me like her bestie!!! Nobody pours a Grand Mariner better than Alice.   What?  They do fancy???   Hell Yes!!  Premium tequilas, good Bourbon, they have it.... but most of all you feel at home, they have very welcoming regulars.   If someone is doing a food run, you will probably be included.   Isn't that what a neighborhood bar should be about??'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-04-15 23:35:01', 'review_text': 'Sometimes YOU "get what YOU pay for" & sometimes YOU get just WHAT you're looking for...!  Especially if it is that "throwback" friendly "tavern" of Ol'!  That The "dufas hipsters" like to refer as a "dive bar", because they have NO reference points in their own generation!

Anyway if YOU are looking for a small, intimate NO FRILLS, friendly lil' place to "toss back a few" w/ your friends and/or solo THIS should be on your "go to LIST"...!!!

Plenty of GOOD restaurants within in walking distance...'}]}

{'name': 'Chick-fil-A', 'address': '3707 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Sandwiches, Chicken Shop, Chicken Wings, Fast Food, Caterers, Event Planning & Services', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '6:30-22:0', 'Wednesday': '6:30-22:0', 'Thursday': '6:30-22:0', 'Friday': '10:30-22:0', 'Saturday': '6:30-16:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-04 06:14:23', 'review_text': "A top tier chick fil a that only appears once in a lifetime. Love the food and service at this location specifically. I know there are many different chick fil a's but this one in particular nails customer service. When they mess up on an order (which they rarely do) they always make sure to make it right! That's customer service which is pretty hard to find in the fast food industry."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-22 05:05:38', 'review_text': 'Love it! Food is awesome every single time but not a big fan of the outdoor cleanliness'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-14 13:39:47', 'review_text': "Delicious as always!
Go to for fast food and the fries never disappoints.

Must try the peppermint milkshake at least once. I don't really even like milkshakes because I prefer to eat and not drink my ice cream, but this one was pretty yummy and I had multiple sips of my partners drink!"}]}

{'name': 'Pressed', 'address': '651 Paseo Nuevo, Ste 305', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Ice Cream & Frozen Yogurt, Juice Bars & Smoothies, Convenience Stores, Vegan, Food, Health Markets, Specialty Food, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-18:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-20:0', 'Friday': '10:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-19:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': None, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-20 00:55:49', 'review_text': 'How is it that Pressed employees are always so unpleasant and unsociable! I met one nice employee my first time at this location who was from San Diego like me. She made conversation and was genuine. My other experiences have been far from this, the employees are agitated and do not make any conversation. Honestly very disappointed because this is the second location I have been to with poor customer service.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-14 16:01:47', 'review_text': 'We happened to drive through SB yesterday and were craving some good juice so we stopped by Pressed. We ordered our usual Berry Smoothies, which were delicious as always.

The only thing that prevents me from giving this location 5 stars... the staff. I walked inside and waited a bit for someone to come out from the back. It took so long that I awkwardly tried to look into the back to see if anyone was there lol. At one point I had to yell out, "hello?" to which a guy came out to help. He wasn't very friendly and seemed a bit annoyed that I came in but maybe it was just a bad day. 

All in all, who knows how many people came in before me and gave up waiting for him.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-08 17:29:57', 'review_text': 'Pressed Juicery is known for their variety of healthy juices from their detox formulations to healthy citrus and greens flavors . They've expanded to what's called  "Freeze" which is their soft serve ice cream  product! Pictured is the chocolate soft serve with chocolate icing frozen on top, sliced strawberries  and coconut  flakes! It was sweet and refreshing with that nice freeze melting in your mouth!'}]}

{'name': "Choi's Oriental Market", 'address': '185 S Patterson Ave, Ste D', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Grocery, Korean, Restaurants, International Grocery', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-19:30', 'Wednesday': '10:0-19:30', 'Thursday': '10:0-19:30', 'Friday': '10:0-19:30', 'Saturday': '10:0-19:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': False, 'street': None, 'lot': True, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 22:24:32', 'review_text': "A must try in Santa Barbara! I've had soondubu many places, but this one is my favorite. I've had the bulgogi, spicy pork, soondunu, tteokmanduguk, and the tteobokki and I would recommend all of them. 

It's a small mom and pop kind of store with various Asian goods run by a husband and wife. They're always super friendly. The husband runs the front and the wife runs the kitchen. The food reminds me very much of when I would go to my korean friends' houses with that kind of home cooking.

Definitely food that warms the soul and fills you up, and for a good price too!"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 04:58:28', 'review_text': 'If I could give zero stars I would.  Wanted to order something off the menu. When I walked up to the counter, the cashier - an older Asian man asked me ''what do you want?"  No pleasant greeting hello of any kind instead he was just extremely curt and lacked any type of of customer service skills.  The woman working the kitchen in the back was just as unpleasant.  I like supporting small local businesses, but the extremely rude staff at this market don't seem to care nor appreciate the business they are getting.  I will NEVER return again and will NEVER waste my time and money here!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-04 04:52:53', 'review_text': 'Great hole in the wall spot for Korean food! This place is really neat and doubles as both a restraint and a mini Korean market. We looked around the market while our food was being prepared and grabbed some ramen and calpico upon finding boReally enjoyed the bulgolgi and the sundubu. With the lack of Korean food in Santa Barbara, the food really hit home!'}]}

{'name': 'Rockfire Grill', 'address': '6583 Pardall Rd', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Chicken Wings, Sandwiches, Breakfast & Brunch, Pizza, Burgers', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '11:30-22:0', 'Wednesday': '11:30-19:0', 'Thursday': '11:30-22:0', 'Friday': '11:30-22:0', 'Saturday': '17:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-22:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 19:02:34', 'review_text': 'Was a nice place good food and good service . Highly recommend. Lots of tvs for sports fans and overall good vibe'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-05 05:57:43', 'review_text': 'I really like Rockfire Grill. We were coming from LA  and stopped by there to grab something to eat. We got pizza, burger, and gyros. My daughter liked the burger. I liked all the food. Our pizza was  burnt at the bottom but they gladly renewed. Great customer service'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-04 23:13:41', 'review_text': "My friend and I stopped in here to grab an outdoor dinner on a beautiful evening and we had a great experience! The patio has plenty of seating, service at the counter and efficient and our cashier gave great recommendations since we had never eaten here before. Loved the vibe, with the kind of surfy decor and a playlist that took me back to the Caribbean.

Let me start with the stars of the meal...the flatbread burger. Why aren't these a thing everywhere because they should be?! I ordered the East Bay BBQ and holy cow was it amazing. Meat was cooked to perfection, the house spread was something special, and the flatbread it came on was so good I basically have no words. My friend got the West Coast and she had the same reaction I did. We stuffed ourselves because it was so tasty. We also had chicken wings (with an absolutely delicious honey garlic sauce) and seasoned fries, both of which perfectly complemented the flatbread burgers.

I would order this whole meal again exactly the same way it was so good. Only wish we had one where I live (hint hint guys, open some more locations further down in SoCal). Already planning to take my boyfriend here next time we take a little day trip up to SB."}]}

{'name': 'Convivo Restaurant and Bar', 'address': '901 E Cabrillo Blvd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Mediterranean, Restaurants, Nightlife, Moroccan, Event Planning & Services, Venues & Event Spaces, Italian', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '15:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-21:0', 'Friday': '7:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': True, 'lot': False, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 17:48:57', 'review_text': 'Good food! We ordered the Margherita pizza and bucatini, both were so tasty. Noodles were al dente and loved the pizza crust. Will order  both entrée again! Definitely recommend.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-29 21:44:13', 'review_text': "We have been big supporters here but I am shocked it when people don't look at the situation with empathy.

We've been coming here for meals throughout the year and forgot to use the Axxess Card. We called up and asked about putting an order in for pick up. We go through all that and I let them know that will be using the Axxess Card finally. They said sorry you have to eat inside. I said we cannot somebody has a compromised system and they are not supposed to be eating indoors at this time given him COVID omicron.   Due to the weather the patio is closed. The manager said they would not make any exception. Even though they can see in the record buck we have been coming here a lot.

I think I even asked about the Axxess and the waiter  didn't know what I was talking about. But bottom line is do you want to work with your customers who are long time supporters or do you say to them well sorry you have to take the risk and eat inside or else we won't honor it. It doesn't make any sense. I'm waiting for the general manager to call me back because Ernesto the manager said well basically ignore your doctors orders and eat inside it if you want the Axxess - we won't make an exception. He didn't put it in those words but I said that's exactly what his messaging is relaying.  The merchants  should spell it out more clearly. Otherwise again we're talking about inaccurate  advertising."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-27 16:37:09', 'review_text': 'Positives: Great ambience, beautiful architecture inside, nicely decorated for Christmas, delicious (not outstanding) Pizzas, good soup;
Negatives: burnt flat bread, bad appetizer ("Carrot") with over cooked veggies and Baba Ghanoush that tasted nothing like a real Baba Ghanoush, and an arrogant server (Phillip) that was too full of himself!!'}]}

{'name': "Renaud's Patisserie & Bistro", 'address': '3315 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'French, Cafes, Restaurants, Breakfast & Brunch, Food, Sandwiches, Bakeries', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '6:30-16:0', 'Wednesday': '6:30-16:0', 'Thursday': '6:30-16:0', 'Friday': '6:30-16:0', 'Saturday': '6:30-16:0', 'Sunday': '6:30-15:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-18 18:26:49', 'review_text': 'Wow wow wow! Stopped here on our way home to OC from Los Olivos and had their croissant egg breakfast sandwich, fresh squeezed OJ and chocolate croissant. Literally BEST. IVE. EVER. HAD! So excited we found a place for breakfast on our way home!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 20:02:25', 'review_text': 'Delicious croissant breakfast sandwich! Friendly staff, cute ambiance, quick service.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-05 17:09:20', 'review_text': "We have enjoyed Renaud's many times, for breakfast, lunch, special desserts or just a snack. But I was really blown away this year by their Galette Des Rois (King's Cake) to celebrate Epiphany (January 6). 

I've had the traditional Mardi Gras style cake many times, either homemade or store bought. However, Renaud's has really WOWED me with the french style King's Cake!! It's everything I love about french pastries, buttery, light, delicious almond filling! It is just fantastic and so fun. 

The cake comes with two adorable little figurines to hide in the cake and a gold crown! It's such a fun cake to share and delicious with coffee. I really enjoyed this seasonal item and I can't wait to order another next year."}]}

{'name': 'The Honey B', 'address': '602 Anacapa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Vegetarian, Gluten-Free, Food, Restaurants, Coffee & Tea, American (New), Vegan, Cafes', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Wednesday': '8:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '8:0-20:0', 'Friday': '8:0-20:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-16:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-09 18:25:10', 'review_text': '"OMG people. Its called The Eggo - sunny side egg, shaved parm, lemon sauce, romaine, tomato, ON SPINACH SUNDRIED TOMATO WAFFLES- GAH! I added carmelized onions and avocado . . ."

This was from a couple of years ago when Honey B was atop Antioch University on  Anacapa Street. It has since closed down, but the chef does pop ups and perhaps has plans to reopen in the future - if she does, we'll soon be regulars again. All of her food is wonderful, super healthy, filling, satisfying, full of deliciousness. We constantly rave about Honey B, and her cookbook has a lot of the recipes from that restaurant. 

Check out her website to see what she's up to now: https://www.thehoneybkitchen.com'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-10-07 10:02:41', 'review_text': "We walked around disoriented and didn't find the cafe. After we sneaked through the building, we finally found it. Little sweet student cafe. I had the best matcha latte I've ever had in my life!!!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-08-11 06:10:00', 'review_text': 'Beyond grateful that I can walk into an eatery and order without stress. So many delicious VEGAN options! The prices are very fair, especially when compared to SB pricing. They even have vegan soft serve. The dillies and mighty bowl are my favorites, but I know I can keep returning for other amazing vegan options. Plus, the rooftop is an amazing place to eat.'}]}

{'name': 'Bettina', 'address': '1014 Coast Village Rd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Italian, Pizza', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '16:0-20:30', 'Wednesday': '16:0-20:30', 'Thursday': '16:0-20:30', 'Friday': '16:0-20:30', 'Saturday': '16:0-20:30', 'Sunday': '16:0-20:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 02:46:25', 'review_text': 'The hype is over for this place. Local, who used to use this place for everything, and a spot to celebrate girlfriends birthdays. The food was not the issue. The staff is flat, unengaging and silent. You can feel their stuffy awkward energy. As someone who used to be a server myself, I always love being courteous to server staff/tipping well. But man, very hard to do here.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-10 20:40:01', 'review_text': "Omg I'm a hard core pizza aficionado and this could be my new favorite pizza place in North America. Don't let it's location in the Montecito Country Mart fool you, please make a reservation asap. 

The menu is very tight but that's fine. Everyone raves about the carbonara pizza but I hate eggs do we skipped it. We wanted a light lunch to save room for steak dinner so we opted for a bottle of Sancerre, baby gems salad and meat lovers pizza. They all hit perfectly!

The server was terrific. The ambiance felt like a garden getaway and parking was too easy. Please run to this lovely restaurant and grab a matchbox or two for the memories."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-06 05:51:02', 'review_text': "Decided to check out Bettina during our recent trip to Santa Barbara and boy was it a great experience. The location is random (in the Montecito country mart shopping center) but the inside and the courtyard of the restaurant are charming. And we figured we came to a good spot when we noticed all the locals either dining there or picking up pies. Everything we ordered was delicious! We got the burrata to start, that had this amazing green pistachio/veggie paste on top - it also came with an excellent Focaccia. Broccolini, which was tangy, charred to perfection and just delish.  And two pizzas, the mushroom and pepperoni, which may have been the best I've had. Great little spot in SB, highly recommend."}]}

{'name': 'Blind Tiger', 'address': '409 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Nightlife, Bars, American (New), Restaurants, Cocktail Bars', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '16:0-1:0', 'Wednesday': '16:0-1:0', 'Thursday': '16:0-1:0', 'Friday': '16:0-1:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-1:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-1:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': True, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-04-10 03:56:06', 'review_text': "Saw the DTease last night and was blown away !! The club is not your usual dive it's has a great design and feel!! The show was amazing with great sound talented artist with great originals can't understand why the place was not sold out !!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-11-01 04:54:45', 'review_text': "First time in Blind Tiger to check out the open mic on Wednesday. Very clean, no rank smell - this is important - and tasteful comfortable furnishings. The stage is very pro w good sound system and lighting. When I went to the bar the server was very friendly and relaxed - I liked that too. Our non-alcoholic drinks were tasty and imaginative and he offered us free refills! Not all the acts were great, but a couple really were good and the in house MC was also a strong performer. We'll be back for sure."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-09-01 16:09:43', 'review_text': "I just moved here and this is my first yelp review. I decided to make one and start with a review of Blind Tiger. I've been to 3 different bars since I got into town and Blind Tiger was definitely my favorite. 

I came on with one of my girlfriends on Saturday. There was a $10 cover but the accommodating staff and great crowd made it all worth it. Brandon was so informative and fun and made our entire experience memorable. 

We will definitely be back to dance and party with everyone!!!!"}]}

{'name': "Rudy's Mexican Restaurant & Take Out", 'address': '811 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Mexican', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2013-02-04 13:52:45', 'review_text': 'Oh man, I love the Energy Burrito with chicken here. It's probably the furthest from authentic you can get, but authenticity doesn't have a monopoly on delicious! I like it so much I simply haven't tried the other options, though I hear they're good (and pretty authentic). 

I would say the consistency isn't the best - sometimes it's a bland or weirdly dry or otherwise "off," but when they do it right it's my second favorite burrito. Love to let the juice from the burrito run onto the tortilla chips that come with...'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-11 18:14:18', 'review_text': "I would go here again but I would stick with a simple chicken taco and nothing that sounds greasy.  The shrimp quesadilla was just too much cheese and greasy.  If that's what you're into then you'll love it.  Probably not the best food choice if you're at all health conscious.  But if you order smart you'll be just fine.  The food is good.  The salsa bar is exceptional.  Fresh everything to suit anyone's needs for whatever plate you order.  You can order a Mexican beer here to go with your meal which is always a plus.  I would recommend, but watch what you order."}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2011-09-04 00:10:38', 'review_text': "Energy burrito - whole wheat tortilla, grilled chicken, jack cheese & romaine lettuce. 

Honestly, the burrito was only okay. If it were for the guacamole sauce, I wouldn't have like it one bit. The chicken was quite spicy (even though it didn't say it was suppose to be spicy) & there wasn't enough romaine lettuce in my opinion. However, each order does come with a side of tortilla chips & the burritos are definitely big enough to feed two!"}]}

{'name': 'Subway', 'address': '3967 State St Space 4, Space 4', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Breakfast & Brunch, Restaurants, Fast Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '8:0-22:0', 'Tuesday': '8:0-22:0', 'Wednesday': '8:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '8:0-22:0', 'Friday': '8:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '8:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '9:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2020-11-02 05:34:38', 'review_text': "My kid loves Subway. I appreciate their wide selection, their consistency, and their price point, which is dirt cheap for SB. Chances are you like it too, or it wouldn't be the largest fast-food franchise in the country by number of stores. I wish there were 3.5 stars, because that seems more fair. 

This shop is tiny and tucked away in the 5 points center. They have a few tables out front, but it's not a great place to eat unless you're really hungry. They are generally very friendly, although one time I forgot to ask for my free cookie up front and they refused to give it to me. Their cookies aren't any good anyways so they can keep it, but it seemed like a silly decision. Maybe I'll get my kid to TP the place when she's a teenager. 

Anyway, Valentinos, South Coast, Sam's, Plaza Deli, and Fresco all have better sandwiches but not as cheap and maybe your kids love Subway too. Certainly a reasonable option."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-04-21 23:17:40', 'review_text': "Sandwiches were really good wasn't expecting much but honestly as blown away keep up the good work"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2016-03-31 19:45:20', 'review_text': "The employees didn't seem to care, they also didn't cut the bread correctly and the sandwich was falling apart. Make the trip to another subway, it'll be worth it."}]}

{'name': 'Hugos Restaurant', 'address': '1049 Casitas Pass Rd', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Asian Fusion, Breakfast & Brunch, American (Traditional)', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '7:0-14:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-14:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-14:0', 'Friday': '7:0-14:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-14:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-14:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': None, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-15 18:08:24', 'review_text': "We almost gave this place a pass - not a lot of upfront charm. But the Yelp reviews were good so we gave it a try. Glad we did! Friendly service as soon as we walked in. Basic breakfast was hot and delicious. I had scrambled eggs (fresh and yummy) with crispy hash browns and sourdough toast. My husband had the veggie scramble (zucchini, red peppers, onion, mushrooms) all fresh and delicious, with the same sides I had. Good cup of coffee, also! We appreciate a hard-working local restaurant and will definitely come back. Four stars just because the ambiance isn't really there. Don't let that stop you from giving this place a try!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-27 01:28:40', 'review_text': "We were coming home from a college visit trip to SLO and UCSB and wanted to hit Carp for breakfast. My kid typed in breakfast and this was one of the first that popped up - thank you Yelp!! Mom and pop-type small strip-mall cafe and we loved it. My wife and kids had pancakes (wife added blueberries) with eggs and I had the French toast. A side of hash browns to share (although we probably didn't need it) - just what the road trip ordered. Super friendly and when the people in front of us didn't need menus because the locals know what they want, it is a good sign. Hard working family, but open from 7am-2pm so it might not be a bad gig.... We will stop there again I am sure."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-09 16:17:22', 'review_text': "Hugo's Restaurant in Carpinteria is THE best breakfast/brunch spot. I especially love their pancakes, stir fried noodles, and chilaquiles! Their menu is so diverse and anyone can find something to their liking. 

The owners are so welcoming and joyful every time I visit. They have been operating for 20+ years! The service is phenomenal; you never have to wait long for your food. 

If you're ever in the area, this is the spot."}]}

{'name': 'Don Q Family Billiard Center', 'address': '1128 Chapala St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Nightlife, Pool Halls', 'hours': {'Monday': '12:0-2:0', 'Tuesday': '12:0-2:0', 'Wednesday': '12:0-2:0', 'Thursday': '12:0-2:0', 'Friday': '12:0-2:0', 'Saturday': '12:0-2:0', 'Sunday': '12:0-2:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'divey': None, 'hipster': None, 'casual': True, 'touristy': None, 'trendy': None, 'intimate': None, 'romantic': None, 'classy': None, 'upscale': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-22 17:31:14', 'review_text': "I've been going to Don Q for 40+ years! While other pool halls have come and gone, Don Q has endured - I think they still have the same 70s-80s rock playlist in the jukebox. They have the highest quality tables and cloth, both bar and regulation size. It's fun and comfortable with the kids, a date, your wife or the guys - never feels seedy or uncomfortable. The beer and snack selection have increased greatly over time, and are downright over the top now. My only wishes: that they still had scoring beads for straight pool, some chalk cones, and didn't require the felt pad under the cue ball at break. Nonetheless, Don Q is the absolute best place to play pool in SB."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-23 23:15:31', 'review_text': "this place is not a real billiards hall. the felt on all the pool tables is in  bad shape & when u ask the owner about it he'll just be rude.! stiix in ventura is where u have to go to play on real billiards tables. the only reason they r still open is because the kids know they can drink there !"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2019-04-22 04:55:17', 'review_text': "The management at Don Q is probably the worst we've ever encountered in any business venue. We visited there after speaking to someone over the phone to discuss a possible opportunity for a large party event. The venue was relatively full but not overwhelming and the individual in charge couldn't take even a minute to talk to us complaining he was too busy; and, he even avoided us even though we waited for a possible 5 minutes of his time. 

Along side this extreme rudeness, the venue allows outside food to be brought in. It wreaked of uncovered food throughout the place. Food on every counter and bar stool. Quite gross. 

I have to say I will never visit Don Q's again. Management is the rudest I've ever encountered and the place smells. They have a lot to learn about running a business and they missed out on a lucrative opportunity."}]}

{'name': 'Night Lizard Brewing Company', 'address': '607 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Breweries, Beer Gardens, Mediterranean, Nightlife, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '12:0-19:0', 'Tuesday': '14:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '15:0-22:0', 'Thursday': '15:0-0:0', 'Friday': '12:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '12:0-0:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': True, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 22:31:18', 'review_text': 'The only hazy on the strip! Much lower key and chill than the other breweries, but still has a couple of tvs to watch the game while listening to some Reggae!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 19:55:20', 'review_text': "A fire pit, live music, delicious beer, and sales that support an eco-friendly, sustainable cause? Fantastic! This was the line on loop in my head a few nights ago at Night Lizard. After several visits to this State Street brewery, I can easily say it's one of my tops. Staff are friendly, beers are tasty, and the vibe--whether sitting indoors or out--is neat. Gotta love all those hanging plants. 

Among beers tried are the Gnatcatcher IPA, Tiger Salamander Saison, and Monkeyflower Double White Ale. All are solid brews. I have yet to sample the food menu from Yona Redz, but look forward to it. 

There's usually room to sit on the outdoor patio, a Covid-safer option that offers great people-watching. I love holding a tulip glass of a tasty beverage, seeing folks passing by and eying the place. Thinking at them 'yes, you do want to stop here!' I smile a bit when someone does."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-01 00:48:08', 'review_text': 'Trivia night is soooo cool. Best kombucha and seltzer. They say the beers are good too!'}]}

{'name': "Javan's", 'address': '938 Embarcadero Del Nrte', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Restaurants, Burgers', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2014-02-25 06:54:05', 'review_text': "Sigh ... Javan's is no more :'(  I miss it already."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2013-09-10 00:43:52', 'review_text': "It perplexes me that this place is always so empty. Honestly it is the best food in IV without a doubt and it's because the owners double as the cooks and are invested in the overall quality of their ingredients and product. They are always entertaining and you could learn a thing or two from just conversing with them during your lunch. Consider helping out this humble mom and pop shop before heading to a big franchise restaurant because they do not compromise anything in their menu and are competitively priced compared to the rest of IV. 

I would recommend the Tuna sandwich for it's delicious combination of dressings and tastiness of the fish. Every bite is savory and leaves you wanting more. You can't go wrong with any of the sandwiches really though."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2013-09-09 04:07:36', 'review_text': "The owners of this place should seriously consider investing in a good quality sign for out front.  Currently they have an unlit vinyl sign so the place is basically unnoticeable, especially at night.  I bet they would really see business improve if they weren't cheap about the sign.

Good sandwiches and chili though."}]}

{'name': 'The Taj Cafe', 'address': '905 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Pakistani, Restaurants, Indian', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:30-22:0', 'Tuesday': '11:30-22:0', 'Wednesday': '11:30-22:0', 'Thursday': '11:30-22:0', 'Friday': '11:30-23:0', 'Saturday': '11:30-23:0', 'Sunday': '11:30-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 2.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-14 09:19:26', 'review_text': 'Great Chicken Tika Masala and even better service! I recommend this place to anyone in SB.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2011-05-16 19:57:02', 'review_text': "I really can't express enough joy about this place being closed.  If you read my original review you'll see what a terrible time we had with the manager and the wait staff. 

Really..no matter how good the food of a place may be..it will always be soured if the customer service provided by the staff is...pardon my bluntness here...utter crap.  This place turned me and the wife off East Indian food for years.  

Closing couldn't have happened to a worse place.. in my opinion.  If it does re-open, I hope its under new ownership who value their customers needs and desires and are cognizant that we have placed like Yelp to express our pleasure or displeasure at the experiences we receive."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2011-02-24 05:34:42', 'review_text': 'worst service ever received- the food is not worth suffering through this aweful service!! server never asked us how our food was-didnt refill water-seemed annoyed and frustrated he was at work- you could receive better service at mcdonalds and i am not kidding at all- obviously based on other reviews this was not just a fluke-apparently this resteraunt does not care about its customers and is fine allowing lazy people to work there and give horrible service and expect everyone just to pay and keep coming- the place should shut down and reopen under new management who know how to run a resteraunt and hire adequate employees! sucks!'}]}

{'name': 'Pacific Crêpes', 'address': '705 Anacapa St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Wine Bars, Restaurants, Gluten-Free, French, Bars, Nightlife, Creperies', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-15:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-15:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-15:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-15:0', 'Friday': '10:0-15:0', 'Saturday': '9:0-15:0', 'Sunday': '9:0-15:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-09-21 13:12:45', 'review_text': 'All their salads are good but my daughter and I loved the Monaco and Celtic salad the best,  and they also have a lot of choices for crepes. Great food, good customer service and reasonable price...I will definitely recommend this place! Keep it up, Pacific Crepes!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-02-17 21:29:46', 'review_text': "We will miss Pacific Crêpes. They were the real thing. The owners were from Brittany, France. When the mother worked there she ONLY spoke French, even if the customers couldn't. I still don't know how much English she could speak. They hosted our French conversation group for many years (we now meet Wednesdays at Arnoldi's; if you speak a little français come join us). Au revoir, PC!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2018-11-26 06:51:57', 'review_text': 'Delicious and unique french cafe.  Wonderful service.  Amazing coffee too.  Try coffee Mocca.

Enjoy!

We will be back!'}]}

{'name': 'The Sportsman', 'address': '1226 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Nightlife, Dive Bars, Sports Bars, Lounges', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '13:0-2:0', 'Wednesday': '13:0-2:0', 'Thursday': '13:0-2:0', 'Friday': '13:0-2:0', 'Saturday': '13:0-2:0', 'Sunday': '13:0-2:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': True, 'Ambience': {'touristy': None, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': True, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': None, 'casual': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-28 02:54:43', 'review_text': "This bar is awesome!  Didn't think much of it at first but our bartender Alice made our experience impeccable. Not only is she a great mixologist, she is down to earth and stole our hearts with her charm.  Thank you for making my birthday one of the most memorable ones.  Best bartender ever!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-09 00:03:34', 'review_text': "My husband Matt B. and I visited the Sportsman a couple weeks ago for a round of beers after dinner on State Street. We'd been to the Riviera the night before, which took over the Sportsman's old location, and were curious about this place, as it was apparently a Santa Barbara spot that had been around for ages. We stopped by around 10:30 on a Sunday night and it was pretty calm, with an unassuming dive bar atmosphere. There weren't a lot of people and we talked to the bartender for a while, a woman who's been with the bar for quite a long time.

We got a couple of draft beers--two IPAs on tap, I think Figueroa Mountain and Firestone--and played a couple rounds of pool. It's a good thing there weren't a lot of people around because we (and me especially) are absolutely dog shit terrible at pool. I was embarrassed that my own husband was there to witness my astounding lack of coordination. Like if someone wanted to blackmail me with the footage, I would probably be willing to pay. We should never do that in public.

Even so, it was fun, and the beer was good and refreshing. We enjoyed our visit to the Sportsman and would be happy to go back for more beer and maybe pool, as long as no one else is watching."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-27 18:51:52', 'review_text': "We love dive bars, especially when the bartender makes bloody Mary's from scratch! No premix crap! It was a Monday morning and the bloody mary really hit the spot. Very small place but clean. Locals spot, friendly people"}]}

{'name': 'Wine + Beer', 'address': '38 W Victoria St, Shop 113', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Wine Bars, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Wineries, Arts & Entertainment, Food, Nightlife, Bars, Beer Bar', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-22:0', 'Friday': '11:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-06-28 06:19:43', 'review_text': 'I just had the best 10 minutes of the past two weeks at Beer and Wine.

Ben, who helped me select wines from 3 continents was the most personable, polite and professional person I have met in a long time.

He really knows his stuff!'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-27 15:55:18', 'review_text': 'I would skip this place - limited selection, careless service and pricey.  Much better options to grab a beer or glass of wine all over Santa Barbara.  It is unfortunate because the Public Market is a great, fun place for lunch and dinner.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-10-04 20:53:47', 'review_text': 'Great place to have a drink with a meal from the public market.  Nice selection of beers and wine on tap.  Had a couple free samples to help us decide.  Great local wines, and a not so local sour!'}]}

{'name': 'Mexican Fresh', 'address': '315 Meigs Rd, Ste F', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Mexican, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2016-03-03 03:37:40', 'review_text': 'Below average. I run errands in this plaza so I stopped in for a burrito. The place screams "clean me." Everything looks tired and dirty. The cashier was ill with a cold. The cook kept telling her not to "talk to me like that. Ever." 

Seemed like a family feud. The young son was chewing on something in front of a TV. wasn't he supposed to be in school?

Burrito was a good size but chicken was a bit chewy and dry. The atmosphere scared me so I won't be going back.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2016-01-19 21:20:25', 'review_text': 'The carnitas is very good, burritos are huge! Good food at a reasonable price. Great salsa selection to go with whatever you order.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2015-12-30 06:18:29', 'review_text': '3.5 stars is accurate. Good, affordable, and fast Mexican food. Love the salsa bar with containers to go!'}]}

{'name': 'Surf Dog', 'address': 'The Bluffs Parking Lot', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Hot Dogs', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2017-02-25 05:41:32', 'review_text': 'He treated me with such respect when stopping for a bite on my cycling and knew just what would be the best for me. So missed before I could turn you onto other fellow friend cyclists.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-02-28 20:34:48', 'review_text': "So sorry to hear Bill passed away. He was the nicest man, kind and thoughtful. We'll miss him"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-02-15 05:17:27', 'review_text': "Bye Bye Bill.... 

A hotdog stand now in heaven to quench the love that is always needed everywhere.  I really will miss you on that corner with your wit and caring banter. 

past review.... AN OASIS ....  Don't drive by without stopping...  Great hotdogs, views, customers are a hoot and Bill has a viable suggestion for any challenge. I met him as he was lecturing in a business class.  An oasis....  Seal Rookery down the trail...  Very COOL"}]}

